COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[333,"§Al-Hajj\ndeeds\nAttend an Islamic study circle, or listen to a recorded one, so that you gain knowledge and guidance.\nSay, \"My Lord, increase my knowledge.\"\nSay, \"O Changer of the hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.\"\nguid\nArguing about the religion without proper knowledge is a sign of ignorance.\nOne of the most severe punishments and deprivation of someone is being at war against the religion and sparing no effort.\nBeware of a sign of hypocrite: Worshiping during times of ease, and apostasy when facing an affliction.\nrefl\nوَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يُجَٰدِلُ فِي ٱللَّهِ بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٖ وَلَا هُدٗى وَلَا كِتَٰبٖ مُّنِيرٖ ٨\nHe does not have the essential knowledge, nor a knowledge acquired through true cognition, nor a knowledge from divine revelation, hence, he is indeed ignorant in all aspects. Al-Shanqiti: 4/280.\nWhen can someone argue about something or have a dialogue?\nثَانِيَ عِطۡفِهِۦ لِيُضِلَّ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۖ لَهُۥ فِي ٱلدُّنۡيَا خِزۡيٞۖ\n(For him in the world is a disgrace), humiliation and shame; since he was too arrogant to heed the signs of Allah, Allah will send humiliation upon him in this world, and will punish him in this world, before he reaches the Hereafter, because this world is all he cares about and all he knows. Ibn Kathir: 3/203.\nA person who becomes arrogant when listening to the Quran will be punished by humiliating him. Why? Why will he be punished in worldly life before the Hereafter?\nوَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يَعۡبُدُ ٱللَّهَ عَلَىٰ حَرۡفٖۖ فَإِنۡ أَصَابَهُۥ خَيۡرٌ ٱطۡمَأَنَّ بِهِۦۖ وَإِنۡ أَصَابَتۡهُ فِتۡنَةٌ ٱنقَلَبَ عَلَىٰ وَجۡهِهِۦ خَسِرَ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَٱلۡأٓخِرَةَۚ ذَٰلِكَ هُوَ ٱلۡخُسۡرَانُ ٱلۡمُبِينُ ١١\nThis verse was revealed because some people would declare their Islam, and if one of them saw good things happening to his wealth and family, he would say, \"This is a good religion\", but if he faced difficulties, he became pessimistic, and would say, \"This is a bad religion\", and renounced Islam. Ibn Juzay: 2/50.\nWhat do you think about one who accepts the religion for worldly gains only?\nخَسِرَ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَٱلۡأٓخِرَةَۚ\nIn regard to this world, this means that they do not get what they hope for by apostatizing. The one who made his apostasy as his asset, giving up his faith in return for something that he thought he would achieve, will find that his efforts were to no avail, and he will not get anything but what is decreed for him. Al-Saadi: 535.\nAn apostate will become a loser in this worldly life. How?\nوَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يَعۡبُدُ ٱللَّهَ عَلَىٰ حَرۡفٖۖ فَإِنۡ أَصَابَهُۥ خَيۡرٌ ٱطۡمَأَنَّ بِهِۦۖ وَإِنۡ أَصَابَتۡهُ فِتۡنَةٌ ٱنقَلَبَ عَلَىٰ وَجۡهِهِۦ\nThat is, among people, some are weak in faith; faith has not truly entered their hearts, and they have never felt the joy of faith. Rather, they entered the religion either out of fear or by way of following a custom, and they cannot be steadfast when faced with trials and tribulations. Al-Saadi: 534.\nWhat is the reason for one's faith to be on the edge and prone to end?\nيَدۡعُواْ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ مَا لَا يَضُرُّهُۥ وَمَا لَا يَنفَعُهُۥۚ ذَٰلِكَ هُوَ ٱلضَّلَٰلُ ٱلۡبَعِيدُ ١٢ يَدۡعُواْ لَمَن ضَرُّهُۥٓ أَقۡرَبُ مِن نَّفۡعِهِۦۚ لَبِئۡسَ ٱلۡمَوۡلَىٰ وَلَبِئۡسَ ٱلۡعَشِيرُ ١٣\n(He invokes one whose harm is closer than his benefit), two questions arise from this verse: First: The idols are described as they can neither harm nor benefit, then they are described as whose harm is closer than their benefit, thus, harm is negated then it is affirmed. This is answered as follows: The negated harm, at first, meant the idols' action, which was nothing because they do not do anything. Second: The second [affirmed] harm meant that they were the cause for the punishment of those who worshiped them, etc. Ibn Juzay: 2/51.\nThe idols are described as they can neither harm nor benefit, and then they are described as whose harm is closer than their benefit. How?\nيَدۡعُواْ لَمَن ضَرُّهُۥٓ أَقۡرَبُ مِن نَّفۡعِهِۦۚ لَبِئۡسَ ٱلۡمَوۡلَىٰ وَلَبِئۡسَ ٱلۡعَشِيرُ ١٣\nThe protector benefits those whom he protects, and the associate brings good to those with whom he is associated, hence, if they fail to do any of that, even in a rare occasion, it would be considered reprehensible, but in this case, they are totally helpless and useless, which makes them the worst protector and associate. Ibn Ashur: 17/216.\nThe idols are the worst protectors and associates. Why?\nwords\nثَانِيَ عِطفِهِTwisting his neck in arrogance\nعَلَى حَرفٍWith doubts and hesitation\nخَيرٌHealth and great wealth\nفِتنَةٌAn affliction with a trial\nالمَولَىىThe protector\nثُمَّ ليَقطَعThen, let him cut off that rope"],[334,"§Al-Hajj\ndeeds\nWhen reciting this verse, prostrate to Allah, realizing that not many people do this prostration.\nInform those around about this fact, which is settled by the Quran: Whomever Allah decrees disgrace upon him, none can honor him. Whoever wants honor, should seek it from Allah.\nSeek refuge with Allah from the torment of Hellfire because it will be unbearable.\nguid\nRemember that guidance is only in the Hand of Allah, hence, do not grieve over those who are disobedient and deniers., and reflect on what Allah has given you of the blessing of guidance.\nReflection on the Quran is the path to guidance.\nAffirmation of the Decree of Allah and His absolute will, thus, He does what He intends, and guides whomever He wills.\nrefl\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَسۡجُدُۤ لَهُۥۤ مَن فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَن فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَٱلشَّمۡسُ وَٱلۡقَمَرُ وَٱلنُّجُومُ\n(The sun, the moon, the stars), these are mentioned by name, because they are worshiped besides Allah, hence, Allah explains that they too prostrate to their Creator and that they are subjected to Him. Ibn Kathir: 3/205.\nThe sun, the moon, and the stars are singled out for mention. Why?\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَسۡجُدُۤ لَهُۥۤ مَن فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَن فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَٱلشَّمۡسُ وَٱلۡقَمَرُ وَٱلنُّجُومُ وَٱلۡجِبَالُ وَٱلشَّجَرُ وَٱلدَّوَآبُّ\nThere is not an inanimate object except that it is obedient, humble, and glorifies Allah, just as Allah says about heavens and earth when they said: (We come willingly) [41:11]. And when describing the stones, Allah says, (And there are some of them that fall down for fear of Allah) [2:74]. Moreover, Allah says, (There is not a single thing that does not glorify Him with His praise, but you do not understand their glorification) [17:44]. Al-Baghawi: 3/206.\nDo all creatures worship Allah? What do we learn from that?\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَسۡجُدُۤ لَهُۥۤ مَن فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَن فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَٱلشَّمۡسُ وَٱلۡقَمَرُ وَٱلنُّجُومُ وَٱلۡجِبَالُ وَٱلشَّجَرُ وَٱلدَّوَآبُّ وَكَثِيرٞ مِّنَ ٱلنَّاسِۖ\nEverything prostrates to His might, willingly or unwillingly, and everything prostrates in a manner that befits its nature. Ibn Kathir: 3/205.\nHow do creatures prostrate to Allah?\nوَمَن يُهِنِ ٱللَّهُ فَمَا لَهُۥ مِن مُّكۡرِمٍۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَفۡعَلُ مَا يَشَآءُ۩ ١٨\nAllah, the Almighty, says that whomever, among His creation, He disgraces and makes him wretched (none can honor him) with blissful life, because all matters are in the Hand of Allah. He guides whomever He wills to His obedience, and forsaken whomever He wills. He distresses whomever He wills, and pleases whomever He wills. (Allah surely does what He wills), Allah does with His creation whatever He wants; He honors whomever He wills, and disgraces whomever He wills because His is the creation and the command. Al-Tabari: 18/587.\nWho, truly, owns the honoring and disgracing? Why?\nفَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ قُطِّعَتۡ لَهُمۡ ثِيَابٞ مِّن نَّارٖ يُصَبُّ مِن فَوۡقِ رُءُوسِهِمُ ٱلۡحَمِيمُ ١٩\nSaeed bin Jubair said: \"Garments of molten copper, which is the hottest of all metals, and they are called garments because they surround the disbelievers from all sides just like clothes.\" Some scholars said: \"The dwellers of Hellfire wear pieces of fire.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/209.\nHow will Hellfire become garments for its dwellers?\nكُلَّمَآ أَرَادُوٓاْ أَن يَخۡرُجُواْ مِنۡهَا مِنۡ غَمٍّ أُعِيدُواْ فِيهَا وَذُوقُواْ عَذَابَ ٱلۡحَرِيقِ ٢٢\nThis verse, (Taste the punishment of the Burning Fire) is similar to this verse (Taste the punishment of the Fire which you used to deny) [32:20]; meaning that they will be humiliated by words and actions. Ibn Kathir: 3/207.\nWhile they will be tortured in Hellfire, they will be told: (Taste the punishment of the Burning Fire). Why?\nوَلِبَاسُهُمۡ فِيهَا حَرِيرٞ ٢٣\nThis is in contrast to the garments of fire worn by the inhabitants of Hell. Ibn Kathir: 3/207.\nWhat is the reason for mentioning the garments in Paradise?\nwords\nوَالصَّابِئِينَSabeans, worshipers of angels or planets\nوَالمَجُوسَMagians, worshipers of fire\nالحَمِيمُA scalding water\nيُصهَرُ بِهِBy which is melted\nمَقَامِعُMaces"],[335,"§Al-Hajj\ndeeds\nTry your best today to speak only good words.\nToday, say this often, \"There is no deity worthy of worship but Allah\", as it is the good word that whoever says it often and adheres to its meaning, will surely dies with it.\nClean a house of Allah (a mosque) in pursuit of divine reward.\nguid\nHonor the Sacred area (the Haram), and beware of intending a sin therein, for you will be held accountable for even thinking about committing a sin.\nEngaging in averting others from the path of Allah entails a severe punishment.\nMosques are founded for worshiping Allah alone, not to be built over gravesites, shrines, or anything that leads to shirk (associating partners with Allah).\nrefl\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ وَيَصُدُّونَ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡمَسۡجِدِ ٱلۡحَرَامِ ٱلَّذِي جَعَلۡنَٰهُ لِلنَّاسِ سَوَآءً ٱلۡعَٰكِفُ فِيهِ وَٱلۡبَادِۚ وَمَن يُرِدۡ فِيهِ بِإِلۡحَادِۢ بِظُلۡمٖ نُّذِقۡهُ مِنۡ عَذَابٍ أَلِيمٖ ٢٥\n(To deviate), to incline from the right thing. (Evildoing), is a general term that varies from disbelief to minor sins, because committing sins in Makkah is more grave than in other places. Moreover, it is said that it means making unlawful acts as lawful. Ibn Juzay: 2/54.\nAllah honors His Sacred House. How does the verse indicate this fact?\nوَطَهِّرۡ بَيۡتِيَ لِلطَّآئِفِينَ وَٱلۡقَآئِمِينَ وَٱلرُّكَّعِ ٱلسُّجُودِ ٢٦\nPurifying the House of Allah is a general command that includes purifying it from disbelief, innovative acts, all impurities and shedding of blood. Al-Qurtubi: 14/359.\nExplain how the House of Allah should be purified.\nوَأَذِّن فِي ٱلنَّاسِ بِٱلۡحَجِّ يَأۡتُوكَ رِجَالٗا وَعَلَىٰ كُلِّ ضَامِرٖ يَأۡتِينَ مِن كُلِّ فَجٍّ عَمِيقٖ ٢٧\nAnd what Allah promised came to pass, people came to it on foot and riding, from east and west. Al-Saadi: 537.\nThis verse contains a Quranic miracle related to informing about the unseen. Explain.\nوَأَذِّن فِي ٱلنَّاسِ بِٱلۡحَجِّ يَأۡتُوكَ رِجَالٗا وَعَلَىٰ كُلِّ ضَامِرٖ يَأۡتِينَ مِن كُلِّ فَجٍّ عَمِيقٖ ٢٧\nThe wisdom behind ordaining the pilgrimage is strengthening the belief in the Oneness of Allah through witnessing the building for which it was established, hence, the meaning of Tawhīd (Oneness of Allah) becomes deeply rooted in the souls that are normally inclined toward physical things. Moreover, mental comprehension is strengthened by witnessing physical signs. Ibn Ashur: 17/243.\nWhat is the wisdom behind ordaining the pilgrimage?\nوَلۡيَطَّوَّفُواْ بِٱلۡبَيۡتِ ٱلۡعَتِيقِ ٢٩\nQatadah said: \"It is called (Freed) because Allah freed it from the destructive hands of tyrants, thus no one of them ever had control over it.\" Sufyan bin Uyaynah said: \"It is called (Freed) because it is never owned by anyone.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/216.\nWhy is the Sacred Mosque called the called (Freed House)?\nذَٰلِكَۖ وَمَن يُعَظِّمۡ حُرُمَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ فَهُوَ خَيۡرٞ لَّهُۥ عِندَ رَبِّهِۦۗ\nMeaning: Whoever avoids disobeying Allah, does not transgress what is sacred and regards committing sin as a very serious matter, then (it is best for him in the sight of his Lord), just as the one who does acts of obedience will earn a great reward, so too, the one who avoids sin will earn a great reward. Ibn Kathir: 3/212.\nHow can a Muslim receive a great reward without, physically, doing something?\nفَٱجۡتَنِبُواْ ٱلرِّجۡسَ مِنَ ٱلۡأَوۡثَٰنِ وَٱجۡتَنِبُواْ قَوۡلَ ٱلزُّورِ ٣٠\nDescribing the idols as \"impure\", because the belief in their divinity constitutes a moral impurity in the souls similar to the clinging of filth to the bodies. Ibn Ashur: 17/253.\nThe idols are described as \"impure\" in this verse. Why?\nwords\nالعَاكِفُ فِيهِThe resident therein\nوَالبَادِThe visitor\nبِإِلحَادٍ بِظُلمٍA deed of deviation\nبَوَّأنَاWe designated\nضَامِرٍA lean camel"],[336,"§Al-Hajj\ndeeds\nWarn other of shirk, and explain its risk.\nPerform prayers in congregation.\nFeed a poor person today.\nguid\nHonor the rites of Allah, inwardly and outwardly, and do not take them lightly.\nMentioning the Name of Allah is the greatest aim of all acts of worship. The servant must constantly remember this great aim.\nDo not detest afflictions that befall you, but endure them patiently for the sake of Allah in pursuit of His reward.\nrefl\nحُنَفَآءَ لِلَّهِ غَيۡرَ مُشۡرِكِينَ بِهِۦۚ وَمَن يُشۡرِكۡ بِٱللَّهِ فَكَأَنَّمَا خَرَّ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ فَتَخۡطَفُهُ ٱلطَّيۡرُ أَوۡ تَهۡوِي بِهِ ٱلرِّيحُ فِي مَكَانٖ سَحِيقٖ ٣١\nIt is said that a polytheist is like one who is falling from the sky in that he is helpless until he hits the ground by the wind, thus, he is doomed, either by being snatched by birds, or falling into a far-off place. Alhasan said: Allah likens the deeds of the disbelievers to this situation in that their deeds become in vain, and they will gain nothing from what they earned. Al-Baghawi: 3/218.\nDescribe the situation of the polytheist in worldly life and in the Hereafter.\nذَٰلِكَۖ وَمَن يُعَظِّمۡ شَعَٰٓئِرَ ٱللَّهِ فَإِنَّهَا مِن تَقۡوَى ٱلۡقُلُوبِ ٣٢\nHonoring: Revering the rites of Allah and aiming for them. It is also said: The rites are all religious matters, and honoring them is performing them with reverence. Ibn Juzay: 2/56.\nHow does the servant honor the rites of Allah?\nذَٰلِكَۖ وَمَن يُعَظِّمۡ شَعَٰٓئِرَ ٱللَّهِ فَإِنَّهَا مِن تَقۡوَى ٱلۡقُلُوبِ ٣٢\nThe intended aim is the piety of hearts toward Allah, and their worship of Him alone to reach total submission to Him. This submission consists of utmost love, humility, and sincerity to Allah, and this is the religion of Abraham (u). All of this indicates that hearts' worship is the fundamental worship. Ibn Taimyah: 4/427.\nHearts' worship is the fundamental worship, how does this verse indicate that?\nفَلَهُۥٓ أَسۡلِمُواْۗ وَبَشِّرِ ٱلۡمُخۡبِتِينَ ٣٤ ٱلَّذِينَ إِذَا ذُكِرَ ٱللَّهُ وَجِلَتۡ قُلُوبُهُمۡ وَٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ عَلَىٰ مَآ أَصَابَهُمۡ وَٱلۡمُقِيمِي ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ وَمِمَّا رَزَقۡنَٰهُمۡ يُنفِقُونَ ٣٥\n(The humble): This trait is followed by four attributes, which are: Their hearts are filled with awe when Allah is mentioned; enduring patiently whatever may befall them for His sake, establishing prayer and spending in His cause. Ibn Ashur: 17/261.\nHumbleness is attained by maintaining four attributes, what are they?\nفَإِذَا وَجَبَتۡ جُنُوبُهَا فَكُلُواْ مِنۡهَا وَأَطۡعِمُواْ ٱلۡقَانِعَ وَٱلۡمُعۡتَرَّۚ كَذَٰلِكَ سَخَّرۡنَٰهَا لَكُمۡ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَشۡكُرُونَ ٣٦\nMeaning: Feed those who ask and those who do not but they show their need, and feed those who never ask and those who do. Ibn Juzay: 2/58.\nIn light of this verse, explain how Islam ensures social security.\nكَذَٰلِكَ سَخَّرۡنَٰهَا لَكُمۡ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَشۡكُرُونَ ٣٦\nAllah has conferred favor upon us by taming these animals and empowering us to control them, despite the fact that they are much bigger and more powerful than we are. This serves as a reminder to the servant that these things are not of his own making, rather, they are what the All-Mighty, the Most Capable wants them to be. The small overpowers the big so that all would know that the Victor is Allah, the One, the Prevailing over His servants. Al-Qurtubi: 14/403.\nDescribe Allah's favor upon His servants by taming these big animals for them.\nلَن يَنَالَ ٱللَّهَ لُحُومُهَا وَلَا دِمَآؤُهَا وَلَٰكِن يَنَالُهُ ٱلتَّقۡوَىٰ مِنكُمۡۚ\nMeaning: You will not attain Allah's pleasure with the meat or the blood, rather, you reach Him with piety, which is sincerity to Him alone in your slaughtering of sacrificial animals. Using this term: (Will not reach) is an affirmation that none of their meat or blood will reach Allah, but only through piety, which is what He wants from you, and will reward you for it. Ibn Juzay: 2/58.\nWhat is the greatest aim for performing the rites of pilgrimage?\nwords\nسَحِيقٍRemote, fatal\nمَحِلُّهَاPlace of sacrifice\nمَنسَكًاA rite of sacrifice\nوَجِلَتThey feared\nصَوَآفَّThey are lined up with one foot tied\nوَجَبَتThey fell down on the ground\nالقَانِعَThe poor who does not beg\nوَالمُعتَرَّThe poor who begs because of need"],[337,"§Al-Hajj\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah to help the oppressed Muslims around the world.\nMaintain your daily prayers, and urge those around you to do the same.\nForbid offensive acts that you see done by your collogues or in your neighborhood.\nguid\nThis is Allah's promise to give His victory to those who support His religion. and hold high His Sharia.\nAllah gives respite to the oppressors, but when He takes them, He does not then let them off.\nWhat is really important is the insight of the heart, not the sight of the eyes. There can be many eye-blinded persons who recognize the facts more than those with good eyes can.\nrefl\nٱلَّذِينَ أُخۡرِجُواْ مِن دِيَٰرِهِم بِغَيۡرِ حَقٍّ إِلَّآ أَن يَقُولُواْ رَبُّنَا ٱللَّهُۗ\nThis is indicative of the wisdom behind Jihad, the purpose of which is to establish the religion of Allah, and stand up to those disbelievers who are persecuting the believers.Al-Saadi: 539.\nThe verse points to one aspect of the wisdom behind ordaining Jihad. Explain.\nوَلَوۡلَا دَفۡعُ ٱللَّهِ ٱلنَّاسَ بَعۡضَهُم بِبَعۡضٖ لَّهُدِّمَتۡ صَوَٰمِعُ وَبِيَعٞ وَصَلَوَٰتٞ وَمَسَٰجِدُ يُذۡكَرُ فِيهَا ٱسۡمُ ٱللَّهِ كَثِيرٗاۗ\nThis verse reinforces the permission to fight, and reveals its benefit. It is as saying: If it was not for the fighting, the disbelievers would have dominated the Muslims and destroyed their religion. Ibn Juzay: 2/59.\nThere is a great wisdom behind Jihad in that it preserves Islam. Explain.\nوَلَوۡلَا دَفۡعُ ٱللَّهِ ٱلنَّاسَ بَعۡضَهُم بِبَعۡضٖ لَّهُدِّمَتۡ صَوَٰمِعُ وَبِيَعٞ وَصَلَوَٰتٞ وَمَسَٰجِدُ\nThis indicates that the countries in which people feel safe to worship Allah, the mosques are maintained, and all the rituals of Islam are established, are part of the virtue resulting from the efforts of those who strive in Jihad, for by virtue of their blessed efforts Allah warded off the disbelievers from that country. Al-Saadi: 539.\nThe Mujahidin do favors for Muslims. Explain.\nوَلَوۡلَا دَفۡعُ ٱللَّهِ ٱلنَّاسَ بَعۡضَهُم بِبَعۡضٖ لَّهُدِّمَتۡ صَوَٰمِعُ وَبِيَعٞ وَصَلَوَٰتٞ وَمَسَٰجِدُ يُذۡكَرُ فِيهَا ٱسۡمُ ٱللَّهِ كَثِيرٗاۗ\nThe meanings of these houses of worship are exclusive to the nations who had scriptures over a long time. No mention is made of Magians or polytheists, because they do not have what needs to be protected; moreover, the mention of Allah is only made by the people who were given divine Sharia. Ibn Atiyah: 4/125.\nThis verse does not mention the houses of worship for Magians or polytheists. Why?\nوَلَيَنصُرَنَّ ٱللَّهُ مَن يَنصُرُهُۥٓۚ\nMeaning: The one who supports Allah's religion and His allies. This is a promise that implies encouragement to fight. Ibn Juzay: 2/59.\nWhat is the pre-condition for achieving victory?\nٱلَّذِينَ إِن مَّكَّنَّٰهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ أَقَامُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَءَاتَوُاْ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ وَأَمَرُواْ بِٱلۡمَعۡرُوفِ وَنَهَوۡاْ عَنِ ٱلۡمُنكَرِۗ وَلِلَّهِ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلۡأُمُورِ ٤١\nWhoever performs these deeds, Allah will give him victory over his enemy. Ibn Taimyah: 4/434.\nWhat are the duties of Mujahidin when they are given authority in the land?\nفَإِنَّهَا لَا تَعۡمَى ٱلۡأَبۡصَٰرُ وَلَٰكِن تَعۡمَى ٱلۡقُلُوبُ ٱلَّتِي فِي ٱلصُّدُورِ ٤٦\nMeaning: The real harm comes from blindness of the heart, as for blindness of the eye, it is harmless to one's religion. Al-Baghawi: 3/224.\nWhat is the harmful blindness that leads to man's demise?\nwords\nصَوَامِعُMonasteries for Christian priests\nوَبِيَعٌChurches for Christians\nوَصَلَوَاتٌSynagogues for Jews\nفَأَملَيتُI gave respite and did not hasten to punish\nخَاوِيَةٌ عَلَى عُرُوشِهَاIn ruins, fallen in upon its roofs\nوَقَصرٍ مَشِيدٍA lofty empty palace"],[338,"§Al-Hajj\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, I seek protection in Your pleasure from Your anger, in Your forgiveness from Your punishment, and I seek protection in You from You. I cannot enumerate Your praises, You are as You have praised Yourself.\"\nTry to recall, over the last week, how many duties you had neglected, and how many sins you had committed, then ask often for Allah's forgiveness so that your heedlessness and hardness of your heart will not be unbridled.\nIdentify three things you feel they soften your heart and act upon them.\nguid\nBe a preacher to Allah, warning others against His punishment, and explaining to people their religion.\nBe keen to rid your heart of lusts and doubts through remembering Allah and seeking knowledge.\nFocus on the deeds of the heart, such as love, fear, and glorification of Allah, etc.\nrefl\nوَكَأَيِّن مِّن قَرۡيَةٍ أَمۡلَيۡتُ لَهَا وَهِيَ ظَالِمَةٞ\nThe fact that they hastened to do wrong does not mean that We should hasten to punish them. Al-Saadi: 541.\nIs the indulgence of the wrongdoer and his sense of security an indication that he is doing the right thing? Explain.\nفَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ لَهُم مَّغۡفِرَةٞ وَرِزۡقٞ كَرِيمٞ ٥٠\nDescribing the provision as (generous) indicates its abundance and worry-free. Ibn Ashur: 17/294.\nWhat does describing the provision as (generous) in the verse indicate?\nلِّيَجۡعَلَ مَا يُلۡقِي ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ فِتۡنَةٗ لِّلَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٞ وَٱلۡقَاسِيَةِ قُلُوبُهُمۡۗ وَإِنَّ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ لَفِي شِقَاقِۢ بَعِيدٖ ٥٣\n(A trial), an ordeal and tribulation. (Sick), doubt and hypocrisy. (Hardened), their hearts repudiate the truth, and they were the polytheists who were tried when they heard that. Al-Baghawi: 3/228.\nWhat types of hearts that are affected by the devil's whispers and become tried?\nلِّيَجۡعَلَ مَا يُلۡقِي ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ فِتۡنَةٗ لِّلَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٞ وَٱلۡقَاسِيَةِ قُلُوبُهُمۡۗ وَإِنَّ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ لَفِي شِقَاقِۢ بَعِيدٖ ٥٣ وَلِيَعۡلَمَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡعِلۡمَ أَنَّهُ ٱلۡحَقُّ مِن رَّبِّكَ فَيُؤۡمِنُواْ بِهِۦ فَتُخۡبِتَ لَهُۥ قُلُوبُهُمۡۗ\n(So that He may make what satan casts a trial), for two groups of people about whom Allah does not care. They are (those whose hearts are sick), which is a weakness or lack of perfect faith and firm belief, hence, the slightest doubt that occurs to them may shake their faith. When they hear what satan throws in, they begin to doubt, and it becomes a test for them. (And those whose hearts are hardened), rigid, not influenced by rebukes or reminders, and they do not understand what Allah and His Messengers say because of their hardheartedness. Hence, what satan throws in becomes a trial of these two groups, thus, exposing what is in their hearts of concealed evil. As for the third group, it is a mercy in their case. They are the ones who are mentioned in this verse: (And so that those who were given knowledge may know that this [Quran] is the truth from your Lord), because Allah has blessed them with knowledge through which they recognize the truth as distinct from falsehood, and guidance as distinct from misguidance. Hence, they distinguish between the two matters. Al-Saadi: 542.\nWhen facing doubts, people become divided into three groups. What are they?\nلِّيَجۡعَلَ مَا يُلۡقِي ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ فِتۡنَةٗ لِّلَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٞ وَٱلۡقَاسِيَةِ قُلُوبُهُمۡۗ وَإِنَّ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ لَفِي شِقَاقِۢ بَعِيدٖ ٥٣ وَلِيَعۡلَمَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡعِلۡمَ أَنَّهُ ٱلۡحَقُّ مِن رَّبِّكَ فَيُؤۡمِنُواْ بِهِۦ فَتُخۡبِتَ لَهُۥ قُلُوبُهُمۡۗ وَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَهَادِ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِلَىٰ صِرَٰطٖ مُّسۡتَقِيمٖ ٥٤\nAllah divided the hearts into three types: Hardened hearts, sick hearts and believing humble hearts. Ibn Taimyah: 4/441.\nAccording to this verse, what are the types of hearts? And how do you classify your heart?\nوَلِيَعۡلَمَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡعِلۡمَ أَنَّهُ ٱلۡحَقُّ مِن رَّبِّكَ فَيُؤۡمِنُواْ بِهِۦ فَتُخۡبِتَ لَهُۥ قُلُوبُهُمۡۗ وَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَهَادِ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِلَىٰ صِرَٰطٖ مُّسۡتَقِيمٖ ٥٤\nWhenever the truth is debated, its proofs become clear, and its arguments get lucid, as Allah says, (He causes many to go astray thereby and guides many thereby)[2:26]. (So they may believe in it), because they realize its truthfulness against the weakness of the raised doubts. (Their hearts become humbled), they find tranquility and submit to it, for Allah comforted their hearts. Al-Biqai: 13/73.\nThe debate between people of truth and others is beneficial to all. Explain.\nوَلَا يَزَالُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ فِي مِرۡيَةٖ مِّنۡهُ حَتَّىٰ تَأۡتِيَهُمُ ٱلسَّاعَةُ بَغۡتَةً أَوۡ يَأۡتِيَهُمۡ عَذَابُ يَوۡمٍ عَقِيمٍ ٥٥\n(A barren Day): The day of the Battle of Badr. It is described as barren day, because the disbelievers were killed and had no day or night afterward. Ibn Juzay: 2/62.\nDescribing the day as barren implies a warning and a threat to the disbelievers. Explain.\nwords\nأَملَيتُ لَهَاI gave them respite\nتَمَنَّىHe recited the revealed verses\nفَتُخبِتَThey become humbled\nمِريَةٍDoubt\nبَغتَةًSuddenly\nيَومٍ عَقِيمٍDay of Resurrection"],[339,"§Al-Hajj\ndeeds\nAbandon bad companions and places of sins, regarding that as a type of emigration for the cause of Allah.\nAfter Al-Fajr prayer, reflect on Allah's power in causing the day to merge into the night.\nWorship Allah using His Glorified Names mentioned here.\nguid\nAllah's praise of those who emigrated and left their land and homes for His cause indicates the risk of residing among the disbelievers.\nKeep in mind that Allah does not forsake His servant when he is subjected to wrong or harm.\nAny call for unity that is not based on Allah's Sharia is false.\nrefl\nفَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمۡ عَذَابٞ مُّهِينٞ ٥٧\n(A humiliating punishment) that will be severe and painful for them, and will reach their hearts. As they tried to humiliate His Messengers, and ridicule His revelations, Allah will humiliate them with the punishment. Al-Saadi: 543.\nHow will Allah punish the criminals with a befitting recompense for their deeds?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ هَاجَرُواْ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ ثُمَّ قُتِلُوٓاْ أَوۡ مَاتُواْ لَيَرۡزُقَنَّهُمُ ٱللَّهُ رِزۡقًا حَسَنٗاۚ\nThose who emigrated for the cause of Allah, and then were killed or died are singled out for mention to allude to the importance of migration for the cause of Allah. Ibn Ashur: 17/309.\nThose who emigrated for the cause of Allah are singled out for mention, even though they are included in the description of the believers in previous verses. Why?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ هَاجَرُواْ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ ثُمَّ قُتِلُوٓاْ أَوۡ مَاتُواْ لَيَرۡزُقَنَّهُمُ ٱللَّهُ رِزۡقًا حَسَنٗاۚ وَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَهُوَ خَيۡرُ ٱلرَّٰزِقِينَ ٥٨\nAllah describes those who left their homes and families for His sake and pleasure, and for fighting against His enemies, then they were killed or died in doing so - that He will provide for them, on the Day of Resurrection, in His Paradise a good provision which is a generous one. Al-Tabari: 18/673.\nWhen is leaving one's homeland considered a good deed?\nذَٰلِكَۖ وَمَنۡ عَاقَبَ بِمِثۡلِ مَا عُوقِبَ بِهِۦ ثُمَّ بُغِيَ عَلَيۡهِ لَيَنصُرَنَّهُ ٱللَّهُۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَعَفُوٌّ غَفُورٞ ٦٠\n(Allah is Ever-Pardoning, All-Forgiving), if it is said: How is mentioning these two of Allah's Names relevant to punishment? The answer is two-fold, first: Mentioning these two names indicates that pardon is better than punishment; it is like a call for pardon. Second: Mentioning these two names indicates Allah's pardon of the wronged person when he retaliates. Ibn Juzay: 2/62.\nThe verse concludes with (Allah is Ever-Pardoning, All-Forgiving). Why?\nذَٰلِكَۖ وَمَنۡ عَاقَبَ بِمِثۡلِ مَا عُوقِبَ بِهِۦ ثُمَّ بُغِيَ عَلَيۡهِ لَيَنصُرَنَّهُ ٱللَّهُۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَعَفُوٌّ غَفُورٞ ٦٠\nThis is how Allah always is, and this is how He deals with His servants at all times, offering pardon and forgiveness. Therefore, you who have been wronged and mistreated should pardon, overlook and forgive so that Allah may treat you as you treated His servants; (Whoever forgives and makes reconciliation, his reward is with Allah) [42:40]. Al-Saadi: 543.\nWhat do you benefit from knowing that Allah is Ever-Pardoning, All-Forgiving?\nذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُولِجُ ٱلَّيۡلَ فِي ٱلنَّهَارِ وَيُولِجُ ٱلنَّهَارَ فِي ٱلَّيۡلِ وَأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ سَمِيعُۢ بَصِيرٞ ٦١\nVictory necessitates the overpowering of one side over the other, and driving one army into the other during battle. It is used here as an example of extending the daytime longer than that of nighttime during some parts of the year, and extending the nighttime longer than that of daytime during other parts of the year. Ibn Ashur: 17/314.\nPeople are changing from victory to defeat. How does this verse exemplify this meaning?\nوَأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ هُوَ ٱلۡعَلِيُّ ٱلۡكَبِيرُ ٦٢\nAs a sign of His pride, the purpose of all acts of worship done by the inhabitants of the heavens and the earth is to magnify Him, glorify Him, venerate Him and honor Him. Hence, Takbir (saying, Allah is Most Great) is the initiation of major acts of worship such as prayer and others. Al-Saadi: 544.\nWhy is Takbir used in the initiation of major acts of worship?\nwords\nمُدخَلًاParadise\nبُغِيَ عَلَيهِHe is wronged\nيُولِجُCauses to enter"],[340,"§Al-Hajj\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah with His Names, (Ever Gracious) and (Most Merciful), so that He may have mercy on you and forgive you.\nAfter waking up from your sleep, say, \"All praise be to Allah who gave me life after having taken it from me, and unto Him is the resurrection.\"\nCall others to Allah by any means you are good at.\nguid\nBeing proud of the religion is a cause for becoming steadfast in it and calling others to it.\nObserve the etiquette of dialogue, as there is a way to answer someone who searches for the truth, and another way to respond to someone who is a stubborn.\nCall others to Allah by any means you are good at.\nrefl\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ سَخَّرَ لَكُم مَّا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَٱلۡفُلۡكَ تَجۡرِي فِي ٱلۡبَحۡرِ بِأَمۡرِهِۦ\nThe sailing of ships is singled out for mention here because it is the manifest of its subjugation, for if it was not for the inspiration to build the ships as such, they would have drowned. Ibn Ashur: 17/322.\nAmong all attributes of ships, the sailing is singled out for mention in this verse. Why?\nوَيُمۡسِكُ ٱلسَّمَآءَ أَن تَقَعَ عَلَى ٱلۡأَرۡضِ إِلَّا بِإِذۡنِهِۦٓۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ بِٱلنَّاسِ لَرَءُوفٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٦٥\n(And He holds the sky), this is a favor from Allah upon the people to keep them safe from what could ruin their lives. (Except by His permission), this is a cautionary alert that induces hope and fear. Ibn Ashur: 17/323.\nThe verse combines hope and fear. Explain.\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ سَخَّرَ لَكُم مَّا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَٱلۡفُلۡكَ تَجۡرِي فِي ٱلۡبَحۡرِ بِأَمۡرِهِۦ وَيُمۡسِكُ ٱلسَّمَآءَ أَن تَقَعَ عَلَى ٱلۡأَرۡضِ إِلَّا بِإِذۡنِهِۦٓۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ بِٱلنَّاسِ لَرَءُوفٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٦٥\n(Indeed, Allah is Ever Gracious and Most Merciful to people), He is more merciful to them than their parents and more than their own selves. Hence, He wants what is good for them, whereas they want what is evil and harmful for themselves. By His mercy, He has subjugated all these things for them. Al-Saadi: 545.\nThe verse ends with (Allah is Ever Gracious and Most Merciful). Why?\nإِنَّ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ لَكَفُورٞ ٦٦\nMeaning: Mankind is ungrateful because he denies the signs that point to the power of Allah and His Oneness. It is also said: Allah says that because most people are ungrateful as He says that in another verse: (And few of My servants are grateful) [34:13]. Al-Qurtubi: 14/442.\nExplain why mankind is described as being ungrateful.\nلِّكُلِّ أُمَّةٖ جَعَلۡنَا مَنسَكًا هُمۡ نَاسِكُوهُۖ فَلَا يُنَٰزِعُنَّكَ فِي ٱلۡأَمۡرِۚ\nMeaning: Do not let those who reject you dispute with you and object to some of what you have brought to them, on the basis of their corrupt thinking, like saying, (Trade is just like usury) [2:275], and similar objections to which there is no need to answer, when they are denying the message. If the one who raises these objections whilst denying the message of the Messenger (ﷺ) claims that he is arguing in order to learn and find the right answer, it should be said to him: What we discuss with you is whether the message is sound or not, otherwise his limiting the discussion to this issue is indicative of his stubbornness and attempts to frustrate you. Al-Saadi: 545.\nThe verse contains guidance on debating those who dispute some Sharia rules. Explain.\nوَإِن جَٰدَلُوكَ فَقُلِ ٱللَّهُ أَعۡلَمُ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ ٦٨\nThis verse contains a good etiquette which is taught by Allah to His servants, when responding to those who quarrel with them in stubbornness, not to answer nor debate them, but respond with this statement that Allah taught His Prophet (ﷺ). Al-Qurtubi: 14/445.\nExplain the etiquette of dialogue with one who argues in stubbornness.\nيَكَادُونَ يَسۡطُونَ بِٱلَّذِينَ يَتۡلُونَ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ءَايَٰتِنَاۗ قُلۡ أَفَأُنَبِّئُكُم بِشَرّٖ مِّن ذَٰلِكُمُۚ ٱلنَّارُ وَعَدَهَا ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْۖ وَبِئۡسَ ٱلۡمَصِيرُ ٧٢\n(Say) O Muhammad to these people, (Then shall I inform you of [what is] worse than that? [It is] the Fire which Allah has promised those who disbelieve), the fire and wrath and torment of Allah are far worse than that with which you are trying to scare the believing allies of Allah in this world. The punishment in the Hereafter for these deeds of yours is worse than that what you do to the believers. Ibn Kathir: 5/396.\nThe verse contains consolation to the oppressed believers and a threat to the wrongdoers. Explain.\nwords\nوَالفُلكَShips\nمَنسَكًاSharia, and worship\nفِي كِتَابThe Preserved Tablet\nسُلطَانًاA proof, evidence\nالمُنكَرَDisgust is apparent on the faces\nيَسطُونَThey attack\nالمَصِيرThe place at which they will end up"],[341,"§Al-Hajj\ndeeds\nIn your prayer today, prolong your bowing and prostration because Allah likes that.\nWhen performing the daily prayers today, be keen to perform the recommended Sunnah prayers as enjoined by Allah.\nHelp a needy person with money, effort, or by meeting his need.\nguid\nWhen you revere Allah in your heart by having love and fear of Him, the rest of your body will revere Him too.\nHold fast to Allah at all times, for whoever holds fast to other than Him, will lose and perish.\nKnow that righteous deeds require striving, patience, sacrifice and hardship, so endure them patiently.\nrefl\nمَا قَدَرُواْ ٱللَّهَ حَقَّ قَدۡرِهِۦٓۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَقَوِيٌّ عَزِيزٌ ٧٤\nThey have not revered Allah the reverence He deserves), those who ascribed partners to Allah did not venerate Him as He should be venerated, for they invoked others besides Him and were not sincere to Him in worship, nor really knew Him. This is similar to saying to someone who fails to treat a great person with respect: You did not give him the recognition he deserves. Al-Tabari: 18/686.\nWhoever circumambulates, offers sacrifices or prays to gravesites, does not revere Allah the reverence He deserves. Explain.\nٱللَّهُ يَصۡطَفِي مِنَ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةِ رُسُلٗا وَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ سَمِيعُۢ بَصِيرٞ ٧٥\nAllah Has chosen Gabriel from the angels, and Muhammad (ﷺ) from mankind. Ibn Taimyah: 4/444.\nDescribe the virtue of the Prophet (ﷺ) in light of the verse.\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱرۡكَعُواْ وَٱسۡجُدُواْۤ وَٱعۡبُدُواْ رَبَّكُمۡ وَٱفۡعَلُواْ ٱلۡخَيۡرَ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ۩ ٧٧\nAfter presenting the proofs to the polytheists, and rebuking them for their misdeeds, this Surah concludes by addressing the believers on what amends their deeds and raises their status. This order of topics indicates that focusing on amending the belief takes precedence over amending deeds. Ibn Ashur: 17/345.\nAmending the belief takes precedence over amending deeds. Explain in light of this verse.\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱرۡكَعُواْ وَٱسۡجُدُواْۤ وَٱعۡبُدُواْ رَبَّكُمۡ وَٱفۡعَلُواْ ٱلۡخَيۡرَ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ۩ ٧٧\nBowing and prostration indicate prayer, and they are singled out for mention because they are the greatest among all other pillars of prayer, for they show humility and submission. Ibn Ashur: 17/346.\nAmong all pillars of prayer, bowing and prostration are singled out for mention here. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱرۡكَعُواْ وَٱسۡجُدُواْۤ وَٱعۡبُدُواْ رَبَّكُمۡ وَٱفۡعَلُواْ ٱلۡخَيۡرَ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ۩ ٧٧\n(Worship Your Lord), this is general for all acts of worship after mentioning prayer which is denoted by bowing and prostrating. Prayer is mentioned first because it is the most important form of worship. Ibn Juzay: 2/65.\nPrayer is mentioned before other acts of worship. Why?\nوَجَٰهِدُواْ فِي ٱللَّهِ حَقَّ جِهَادِهِۦۚ\nStriving means doing one's utmost to attain the desired goal. Striving in the cause of Allah as one ought to strive means complying in full with the commands of Allah, and calling people to His path by all possible means, such as offering sincere advice, teaching, fighting, disciplining, rebuking, exhorting, and so on. Al-Saadi: 547.\nIs Jihad limited to carrying weapons to ward off the enemy?\nهُوَ ٱجۡتَبَىٰكُمۡ وَمَا جَعَلَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ فِي ٱلدِّينِ مِنۡ حَرَجٖۚ\nAllah says, with a confirmed negation, that He has not placed upon us in the religion any difficulty. Whoever believes that there is an atom weight of difficulty in what Allah ordains, then he denies Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ). Then, how about one who believes that what is been ordained by Allah is harmful and with no benefit to us? Ibn Taimyah: 4/448.\nThere is no difficulty or harm in what Allah Has ordained . Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nالطَّالِبُThe false deity who lost something to the fly\nوَالمَطلُوبThe fly\nمَا قَدَرُواThey have not revered\nيَصطَفِيHe chooses\nاجتَبَاكُمHe has chosen you\nمِلَّةَ أَبِيكُمThis religion of your father [Abraham (u)]\nمَولاَكُمHe is your protector and helper"],[342,"§Al-Mu'minun\ndeeds\nIdentify three things that make you humble in prayer, and apply them in your prayer today.\nIn your gathering with others today, aim to change ill speech to a beneficial one.\nTry to lower your gaze, as it helps guard your chastity.\nguid\nAllah promises those who bear these qualities with success in this worldly life and the Hereafter.\nTrustworthiness is a great quality, so maintain it.\nIn order to succeed, maintain your daily prayers on time.\nrefl\nقَدۡ أَفۡلَحَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ ١ ٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ فِي صَلَاتِهِمۡ خَٰشِعُونَ ٢ إلى قوله تعالى ٱلَّذِينَ يَرِثُونَ ٱلۡفِرۡدَوۡسَ هُمۡ فِيهَا خَٰلِدُونَ ١١\nAllah says that these believers will inherit Al-Firdaws (The Highest level in Paradise), which entails that others will not. This proves that maintaining these qualities is mandatory. If this were voluntary, then they would have inherited Al-Firdaws without maintaining these qualities, but inheriting Paradise is attained only by doing what is mandatory; hence, no recommended quality is mentioned here. Since humbleness in prayer is mandatory, then it implies tranquility and modesty altogether. Ibn Taimyah: 4/454.\nAccording to this verse, humbleness in prayer is mandatory. How?\nٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ فِي صَلَاتِهِمۡ خَٰشِعُونَ ٢\nHumbleness in prayer is the essence and purpose of prayer, and this is what will be written down in the individual's record. With regard to prayer in which there is no humility and attentiveness of the mind, even though it may be valid and rewardable, the reward for it will be commensurate with the person's level of focus and understanding of what he says. Al-Saadi: 547-548.\nAmong the pillars and duties of prayer, humbleness is singled out for mention. Why?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ عَنِ ٱللَّغۡوِ مُعۡرِضُونَ ٣\nAmong the qualities of successful believers mentioned in this verse is turning away from ill speech, which is, in essence, words and actions that are vain. These include amusement, diversion, larking around and that which is resented by good sense. Al-Shanqiti: 5/306.\nReducing the time spent on useless programs on mobile phones and computers can lead one to success. Explain in light of this verse.\nقَدۡ أَفۡلَحَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ ١ ٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ فِي صَلَاتِهِمۡ خَٰشِعُونَ ٢ وَٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ عَنِ ٱللَّغۡوِ مُعۡرِضُونَ ٣ وَٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ لِلزَّكَوٰةِ فَٰعِلُونَ ٤ وَٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ لِفُرُوجِهِمۡ حَٰفِظُونَ ٥\nHere, Allah praises and commends His believing servants, highlighting their success and bliss, and how they attain success. This implicitly urges us to acquire the same characteristics and encourages us to do so. So, the individual should assess himself and others, measuring against these standards; thus, he will know what he and others have of faith, and the level and extent of that faith. Al-Saadi: 547.\nHow can one identify his flaw so that he can rectify it?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ لِأَمَٰنَٰتِهِمۡ وَعَهۡدِهِمۡ رَٰعُونَ ٨\nTrust and pledge include every obligation man acts upon by words or actions in his religious and worldly affairs. This covers all dealings and appointments with others, etc. The objective is to preserve and fulfill. Al-Qurtubi: 15/15.\nExplain the concept of trust that the servant must maintain.\nوَٱلَّذِينَ هُمۡ عَلَىٰ صَلَوَٰتِهِمۡ يُحَافِظُونَ ٩\nMaintaining the prayer is to perform it on time while fulfilling its conditions. If someone asks: Why does the mention of prayer appear at the beginning of this Surah and in this verse? The answer is: It is not a repetition because humbleness in prayer is mentioned at the beginning and maintenance of prayer is mentioned in this verse, so they are two different things. Ibn Juzay: 2/68.\nAllah mentions prayer at the beginning of this Surah and in this verse. Why?\nوَلَقَدۡ خَلَقۡنَا فَوۡقَكُمۡ سَبۡعَ طَرَآئِقَ وَمَا كُنَّا عَنِ ٱلۡخَلۡقِ غَٰفِلِينَ ١٧\nThe majority of Quran interpreters said that it means that we are aware of the safety of all the creation, lest the heavens fall and cause their destruction. Al-Qurtubi: 15/22.\nDescribe one aspect of Allah's mercy toward His servants.\nwords\nأَفلَحَSucceeded\nاللَّغوWords and actions that are vain\nرَاعُونَFaithful, protective\nنُطفَةًA sperm-drop\nقَرَارٍ مَكِينِThe womb of the woman\nعَلَقَةًA clinging clot\nمُضغَةًA lump of flesh as big as a bite size\nسَبعَ طَرَائِقَSeven layered heavens"],[343,"§Al-Mu'minun\ndeeds\nWhen you drink and wash up today, remember that the blessing of fresh water is the most abundant of worldly blessings of Allah upon us, so thank Him often for it.\nInclude olive oil in your food menu today, as it comes from a blessed tree and it has many benefits.\nWhen mounting an animal, say, \"Glory be to Him Who has subjected this for us, for we could not have done it by ourselves, and indeed, to our Lord, we will surely return.\"\nguid\nWorship Allah often with sincerity.\nThe eminent people in the community are influential leaders in good or evil, so, let us help make them righteous.\nDo not rely on your lineage, for it will not protect you from Allah's punishment.\nrefl\nوَأَنزَلۡنَا مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَآءَۢ بِقَدَرٖ فَأَسۡكَنَّٰهُ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِۖ وَإِنَّا عَلَىٰ ذَهَابِۢ بِهِۦ لَقَٰدِرُونَ ١٨\nAllah says: We can surely take the water away, and you, people, would die of thirst; your land would be ruined, where no vegetation or plants would grow, and your animals would perish. He says: Because of my blessing, the water will be left running for you in the ground. Al-Tabari: 19/20.\nWhat is the source of ground water?\nوَأَنزَلۡنَا مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَآءَۢ بِقَدَرٖ\nMeaning: According to what is needed, not so much that it damages the lands and buildings, and not so little to be insufficient for crops and fruits, but whatever is needed for irrigation, drinking, and other benefits. Ibn Kathir: 3/235.\nSending down water in due measure is a blessing. Why?\nوَإِنَّا عَلَىٰ ذَهَابِۢ بِهِۦ لَقَٰدِرُونَ ١٨\nAllah reminds His servants to show gratitude to Him for His blessings and that they should reflect on the resulting harm if they were to lose these blessings. Al-Saadi: 549.\nThe verse indicates a way by which people know the reality of blessings. What is it?\nوَشَجَرَةٗ تَخۡرُجُ مِن طُورِ سَيۡنَآءَ تَنۢبُتُ بِٱلدُّهۡنِ وَصِبۡغٖ لِّلۡأٓكِلِينَ ٢٠ وَإِنَّ لَكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمِ لَعِبۡرَةٗۖ نُّسۡقِيكُم مِّمَّا فِي بُطُونِهَا وَلَكُمۡ فِيهَا مَنَٰفِعُ كَثِيرَةٞ وَمِنۡهَا تَأۡكُلُونَ ٢١\n(And there is certainly a lesson for you in livestock animals), this is a mention of the blessings that come to them from animals after mentioning what comes from water and plants. Al-Alusi: 9/225.\nThe mention of the blessings of water and plants precedes that of animals. Why?\nفَقَالَ ٱلۡمَلَؤُاْ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ مِن قَوۡمِهِۦ مَا هَٰذَآ إِلَّا بَشَرٞ مِّثۡلُكُمۡ يُرِيدُ أَن يَتَفَضَّلَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ وَلَوۡ شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ لَأَنزَلَ مَلَٰٓئِكَةٗ مَّا سَمِعۡنَا بِهَٰذَا فِيٓ ءَابَآئِنَا ٱلۡأَوَّلِينَ ٢٤ إِنۡ هُوَ إِلَّا رَجُلُۢ بِهِۦ جِنَّةٞ\nThe arguments they gave are rather self-contradictory and flimsy in and of themselves. By saying, (This is not but a man like yourselves who wishes to take precedence over you), they affirmed that he was a man of rational thinking, who was scheming against them in order to put himself above them and become their leader. Moreover, there was a need to warn against him so that no one would be deceived by him. How could that be in harmony with their other argument against him, when they said: (He is not but a man possessed with madness)?! Al-Saadi: 550.\nShow the contradiction in their statements.\nفَقَالَ ٱلۡمَلَؤُاْ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ مِن قَوۡمِهِۦ مَا هَٰذَآ إِلَّا بَشَرٞ مِّثۡلُكُمۡ يُرِيدُ أَن يَتَفَضَّلَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ وَلَوۡ شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ لَأَنزَلَ مَلَٰٓئِكَةٗ مَّا سَمِعۡنَا بِهَٰذَا فِيٓ ءَابَآئِنَا ٱلۡأَوَّلِينَ ٢٤\nThey ruled out the possibility that a Prophet can be human, yet, they proclaimed a stone as a god! Ibn Juzay: 2/70.\nThere is a contradiction in the disbelievers' dismissal of the possibility that a Prophet can be human. Explain.\nفَقَالَ ٱلۡمَلَؤُاْ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ مِن قَوۡمِهِۦ مَا هَٰذَآ إِلَّا بَشَرٞ مِّثۡلُكُمۡ يُرِيدُ أَن يَتَفَضَّلَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ وَلَوۡ شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ لَأَنزَلَ مَلَٰٓئِكَةٗ مَّا سَمِعۡنَا بِهَٰذَا فِيٓ ءَابَآئِنَا ٱلۡأَوَّلِينَ ٢٤\nThe chiefs of the people thought that he brought the message, seeking to be superior to people, thus, they were concerned about their high positions. In fact, because of their ignorance, they did not reflect on what was good for the people; rather, they judged others based on their selfish standards. Ibn Ashur: 18/42.\nThe love for headship is a risk to a person and his faith. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nبِالدُّهنِWith oil\nوَصِبغٍCondiments\nبِأَعيُنِنَاUnder Our Eyes [observation and care] This confirms a physical attribute, [the eyes] to Allah in a manner befitting to Him, the Exalted, not similar to anything in other beings\nوَفَارَ التَّنُّورُWater flows from the oven\nفَاسلُك فِيهَاTake on board\nسَبَقَ عَلَيهِ القَولُThose who deserved punishment"],[344,"§Al-Mu'minun\ndeeds\nRecall a risky situation from which Allah saved you, and praise Him for that.\nSeek refuge with Allah from being distracted by the luxury from His obedience and being close to Him.\nIdentify something that you wanted, but it was hard to achieve, then humbly invoke Allah and ask Him to ease it for you.\nguid\nWhen you survive a disaster or a wrongdoing by an oppressor, do not forget to praise Allah, the Almighty.\nIt is important to reflect and ponder the stories of the Messengers in the Quran, as Allah mentioned them because of their lessons and admonitions.\nThe end of wrongdoers is near, even if it takes a long time.\nrefl\nفَإِذَا ٱسۡتَوَيۡتَ أَنتَ وَمَن مَّعَكَ عَلَى ٱلۡفُلۡكِ فَقُلِ ٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِي نَجَّىٰنَا مِنَ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٢٨ وَقُل رَّبِّ أَنزِلۡنِي مُنزَلٗا مُّبَارَكٗا وَأَنتَ خَيۡرُ ٱلۡمُنزِلِينَ ٢٩\nAllah commanded Noah (u), when he boarded the ship, to praise Him for saving him from the wrongdoers. Then, He commanded him to supplicate Him for a blessed landing. Ibn Atiyah: 4/142.\nWhat are the types of supplications mentioned in this verse?\nفَإِذَا ٱسۡتَوَيۡتَ أَنتَ وَمَن مَّعَكَ عَلَى ٱلۡفُلۡكِ فَقُلِ ٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِي نَجَّىٰنَا مِنَ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٢٨\nAl-Khafaji said: \"This indicates that no one should feel pleasure for another person's calamity, even if he is an enemy, just for the fact that he is struck with it; rather, it should be for being safe from his enemy's harm or for cleansing the land from the dirt of his shirk and misguidance.\" Al-Alusi: 9/230.\nAccording to this verse, there is a difference between victory for oneself and defending the religion. Explain.\nوَقُل رَّبِّ أَنزِلۡنِي مُنزَلٗا مُّبَارَكٗا وَأَنتَ خَيۡرُ ٱلۡمُنزِلِينَ ٢٩\nIn general, through this verse, Allah educates His servants to say this supplication whenever they are on board something or when they get off board. Moreover, they should say it whenever they enter their homes and after greeting. Al-Qurtubi: 15/37.\nWhat is the practical benefit of this verse?\nوَقَالَ ٱلۡمَلَأُ مِن قَوۡمِهِ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ وَكَذَّبُواْ بِلِقَآءِ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ وَأَتۡرَفۡنَٰهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا مَا هَٰذَآ إِلَّا بَشَرٞ مِّثۡلُكُمۡ يَأۡكُلُ مِمَّا تَأۡكُلُونَ مِنۡهُ وَيَشۡرَبُ مِمَّا تَشۡرَبُونَ ٣٣\nThese two traits of the eminent of the people point to the motive for denying their Messenger. Since their denial of the meeting of the Hereafter relieves them from expecting reckoning after death, and their wealth and luxury lure them into arrogance and insolence because they were used to being leaders, not followers. Ibn Ashur: 18/52.\nThe denial of the meeting of the Hereafter and life of luxury are the biggest reasons for detesting the truth and denying the messengers. Explain.\nوَقَالَ ٱلۡمَلَأُ مِن قَوۡمِهِ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ وَكَذَّبُواْ بِلِقَآءِ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ وَأَتۡرَفۡنَٰهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا مَا هَٰذَآ إِلَّا بَشَرٞ مِّثۡلُكُمۡ يَأۡكُلُ مِمَّا تَأۡكُلُونَ مِنۡهُ وَيَشۡرَبُ مِمَّا تَشۡرَبُونَ ٣٣\nThis describes one of the recurring human tendencies where those who are eminent among people are the first ones to reject the message of truth. Al-Jaza'iri: 3/513.\nIn light of this verse, explain the risk of the life of luxury.\nأَيَعِدُكُمۡ أَنَّكُمۡ إِذَا مِتُّمۡ وَكُنتُمۡ تُرَابٗا وَعِظَٰمًا أَنَّكُم مُّخۡرَجُونَ ٣٥ ۞هَيۡهَاتَ هَيۡهَاتَ لِمَا تُوعَدُونَ ٣٦\nMeaning: It is far, far what he promises you of resurrection after you have disintegrated and become dust and bones. Their view was flawed because they came to this conclusion based on their abilities where they compared the ability of the Creator to their own. Exalted be Allah far above that. Al-Saadi: 551.\nThese disbelievers made a mistake for which they denied the resurrection. What was it?\nقَالَ رَبِّ ٱنصُرۡنِي بِمَا كَذَّبُونِ ٣٩ قَالَ عَمَّا قَلِيلٖ لَّيُصۡبِحُنَّ نَٰدِمِينَ ٤٠\nMeaning: Allah said to this supplicant Prophet: In a little while, your people will regret their disbelief, but their regret will be of no avail. Ibn Atiyah: 4/144.\nThe prayer of appressed righteous people is swiftly answered. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nلَـمُبتَلِينWe are ever testing\nقَرنًاA generation of people\nالمَلأُ مِن قَومِهِThe eminent among his people\nهَيهَاتَVery far-fetched\nغُثَاءًLike a froth floating over waters"],[345,"§Al-Mu'minun\ndeeds\nSeek refuge with Allah from arrogance, for it turns one from accepting the truth.\nReview the food items that you consume, and if you find an unlawful item, refrain from it, so that your supplication will be answered.\nShare a message in which you warn against causes of division and dispute in religion.\nguid\nEating only lawful things and engaging in doing righteous deeds are among the reasons for happiness.\nTake heed, lest the blessings you are given lead you gradually to your doom.\nDo not be deluded by your righteous deeds, rather, be constantly fearful of Allah.\nrefl\nإِلَىٰ فِرۡعَوۡنَ وَمَلَإِيْهِۦ فَٱسۡتَكۡبَرُواْ وَكَانُواْ قَوۡمًا عَالِينَ ٤٦\nThey were too arrogant to accept the message of Moses (u), his signs and proofs, and that was because arrogance stemmed from their innate character of haughtiness. Ibn Ashur: 18/64.\nWhat caused Pharaoh and his people to go astray?\nوَجَعَلۡنَا ٱبۡنَ مَرۡيَمَ وَأُمَّهُۥٓ ءَايَةٗ\nAllah says that He made His servant and Messenger Jesus (u) and his mother Mary (o) as a sign for mankind, a definitive proof of His ability to do whatever He wills. For He created Adam (u) without a father or a mother, He created Eve from a male without a female, He created Jesus (u) from a female without a male, and He created the rest of mankind from both male and female. Ibn Kathir: 3/238.\nJesus (u) and his mother Mary (o) are a sign for mankind. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلرُّسُلُ كُلُواْ مِنَ ٱلطَّيِّبَٰتِ وَٱعۡمَلُواْ صَٰلِحًاۖ إِنِّي بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ عَلِيمٞ ٥١\nEating lawful things is mentioned first because it helps in doing righteous deeds. It is narrated in an authentic Hadith that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"Hell is more fitting for all flesh which has grown out of what is unlawful.\" Al-Alusi: 9/241.\nEating lawful things is mentioned first. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلرُّسُلُ كُلُواْ مِنَ ٱلطَّيِّبَٰتِ وَٱعۡمَلُواْ صَٰلِحًاۖ إِنِّي بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ عَلِيمٞ ٥١\nIn Sahih Al-Bukhari and Sahih Muslim, Abu Huraira (t) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \"Allah, the Almighty, is Good and accepts only that which is good, and He has commanded the believers to do that which He has commanded the Messengers. So, the Almighty said: (O messengers, eat from the lawful things and act righteously) and (O you who believe, eat of the lawful things that We have provided you) [2:172]. Then, he (ﷺ) mentioned [the case] of a man who, having journeyed far, is disheveled and dusty, and who spreads out his hands to the sky saying, \"O Lord! O Lord!,\" while his food is haram (unlawful), his drink is haram, his clothing is haram, and he has been nourished with haram, so how can [his supplication] be answered.\" Al-Qurtubi: 12/172.\nWhat is meant by (lawful things) in this verse?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلرُّسُلُ كُلُواْ مِنَ ٱلطَّيِّبَٰتِ وَٱعۡمَلُواْ صَٰلِحًاۖ\nAllah commands His servants and Messengers (p) to eat lawful food and do righteous deeds, which indicates that eating what is lawful helps one to do righteous deeds. Ibn Kathir: 3/239.\nWhat is the link between eating lawful food and doing righteous deeds?\nفَتَقَطَّعُوٓاْ أَمۡرَهُم بَيۡنَهُمۡ زُبُرٗاۖ كُلُّ حِزۡبِۢ بِمَا لَدَيۡهِمۡ فَرِحُونَ ٥٣\nAfter they were commanded to unite, they turned their religion into many factions. Allah mentions that each one of them is obstinate in his views and straying, which is the ultimate misguidance. Al-Qurtubi: 15/52.\nIn light of this verse, explain the risk of division and obstinance in opinion.\nأَيَحۡسَبُونَ أَنَّمَا نُمِدُّهُم بِهِۦ مِن مَّالٖ وَبَنِينَ ٥٥ نُسَارِعُ لَهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡخَيۡرَٰتِۚ بَل لَّا يَشۡعُرُونَ ٥٦\nMeaning: Do these deluded people think that what We give them of wealth and children is because they are honored and precious in Our sight? No, the matter is not as they claim. Their thinking is wrong, and their hopes will be dashed. We only do that to give them respite, and let them go further [in sin]. Ibn Kathir: 3/240.\nAllah gives the wrongdoers wealth and children. Why?\nwords\nأَجَلَهَاIts appointed time of termination\nتَترَاIn succession\nرَبوَةٍA high ground\nذَاتِ قَرَارٍA level area for settling\nوَمَعِينٍFlowing water\nفَتَقَطَّعُواThey divided their religion\nزُبُرًاFactions\nغَمرَتِهِمMisguidance, ignorance"],[346,"§Al-Mu'minun\ndeeds\nChoose an act of worship, then hasten and be the foremost in doing it.\nAs you have a daily time for reading or memorizing the Quran, set up another time for reflecting on the verses of the Quran.\nRead a book about the qualities of the Prophet (ﷺ).\nguid\nRemind yourself constantly of your standing before Allah on the Day of Resurrection.\nSins are the cause for the obliviousness of the heart and leaving it in disarray, while refraining from sins is a cause for the soundness of the heart.\nIgnorance, intolerance, and blind imitation are causes for people's turning away from the truth.\nrefl\nوَٱلَّذِينَ يُؤۡتُونَ مَآ ءَاتَواْ وَّقُلُوبُهُمۡ وَجِلَةٌ أَنَّهُمۡ إِلَىٰ رَبِّهِمۡ رَٰجِعُونَ ٦٠\nVisible deeds are assessed/rewarded commensurate with the levels of faith in the hearts. Faith levels in the hearts vary, and no one knows the levels of faith in the hearts except Allah. Ibn Taimyah: 4/461.\nDraw two benefits from this verse.\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ يُسَٰرِعُونَ فِي ٱلۡخَيۡرَٰتِ وَهُمۡ لَهَا سَٰبِقُونَ ٦١ وَلَا نُكَلِّفُ نَفۡسًا إِلَّا وُسۡعَهَاۚ\nBecause Allah mentioned their hastening to do good and their being foremost in that regard, some people may think that what is required of them and others is something too difficult and hard, so, Allah says, (And We do not burden a soul more than what it can bear). Al-Saadi: 554.\nHastening to do good may become burdensome. How does this verse deal with this issue?\nقَدۡ كَانَتۡ ءَايَٰتِي تُتۡلَىٰ عَلَيۡكُمۡ فَكُنتُمۡ عَلَىٰٓ أَعۡقَٰبِكُمۡ تَنكِصُونَ ٦٦\n(But you used to turn back on your heels), you went backwards. By following the Quran, they could have advanced, but by turning away from it, they went backwards and became the lowest of the low. Al-Saadi: 555.\nIn this verse, there is an indication that making Sharia the law of the land is the best way for progress and development. Explain.\nأَفَلَمۡ يَدَّبَّرُواْ ٱلۡقَوۡلَ\nQatadah said: \"By Allah, if the people had pondered its meaning and understood it properly, they would have found in the Quran a deterrent to disobeying Allah but they only focused on the unspecific verses which are not entirely clear, and so they went astray.\" Ibn Kathir: 3/242.\nWhat is the benefit of urging them to ponder the Quran?\nأَمۡ لَمۡ يَعۡرِفُواْ رَسُولَهُمۡ فَهُمۡ لَهُۥ مُنكِرُونَ ٦٩\nIbn Abbas (k) said: \"Did they not know Muhammad as a child and a grown-up, did they not know his lineage, honesty, trustworthiness, and his truthfulness to his covenants.\" This is a rebuke to the disbelievers for turning away after knowing his truthfulness and honesty. Al-Baghawi: 3/252.\nStudying the Prophetic biography, and learning about the Prophet's (ﷺ) qualities is important. Explain.\nأَمۡ يَقُولُونَ بِهِۦ جِنَّةُۢۚ بَلۡ جَآءَهُم بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَأَكۡثَرُهُمۡ لِلۡحَقِّ كَٰرِهُونَ ٧٠\nAversion to the truth is attributed to most, but not all, of the polytheists. That is in fairness to some, among them with sensible minds who knew the falsehood of shirk, and were inclining to the truth, but they had to go along with the tyrants of their people in order to maintain their safety and livelihood. Ibn Ashur: 18/91.\nAversion to the truth is attributed to most, but not all, of the polytheists. Why?\nوَلَوِ ٱتَّبَعَ ٱلۡحَقُّ أَهۡوَآءَهُمۡ لَفَسَدَتِ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتُ وَٱلۡأَرۡضُ وَمَن فِيهِنَّۚ بَلۡ أَتَيۡنَٰهُم بِذِكۡرِهِمۡ فَهُمۡ عَن ذِكۡرِهِم مُّعۡرِضُونَ ٧١\n(Were the Truth to follow their desires), if the truth follows what people desire and lust for, the world order will be nullified, because people's desires are different and go against each other. In essence, the truth is to be followed, and people should adhere to it. Al-Qurtubi: 15/72.\nThere are limits to freedom. What will happen if these limits are removed?\nwords\nوَجِلَةٌAfraid of not being accepted\nغَمرَةٍ مِن هَذَاOblivious to the Quran\nيَجأَرُونَCrying loudly and humbly\nعَلَى أَعقَابِكُم تَنكِصُونَTurning away from listening to Quran like one turning back on his heels\nسَامِرًا تَهجُرُونَSpending night in evil talks"],[347,"§Al-Mu'minun\ndeeds\nRecall an adversity that Allah relieved for you, and thank Him for it.\nSupplicate Allah, in humility, to relieve Muslims from adversities and harm.\nRead and ponder the blessing of hearing, sight, or intellect, then thank Allah for it.\nguid\nIf you encounter a prolonged trial, increase your worship of Allah with humbleness, and supplicate Him in humility.\nPersisting on sins results in a greater punishment, so beware of that.\nPeople are often deluded by Allah's forbearance.\nrefl\nوَلَوۡ رَحِمۡنَٰهُمۡ وَكَشَفۡنَا مَا بِهِم مِّن ضُرّٖ لَّلَجُّواْ فِي طُغۡيَٰنِهِمۡ يَعۡمَهُونَ ٧٥\nAllah says: If We were to show mercy to those who disbelieve in the Hereafter and end the drought, barrenness and hardship of hunger (they would still persist in their transgression), they would still persist in their insolence and lack of reserve toward their Lord. (Wandering blindly), means hesitating. Al-Tabari: 19/59.\nWhen the disbelievers are punished with adversity in worldly life, it will not be lifted. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَلَقَدۡ أَخَذۡنَٰهُم بِٱلۡعَذَابِ فَمَا ٱسۡتَكَانُواْ لِرَبِّهِمۡ وَمَا يَتَضَرَّعُونَ ٧٦\nAllah says: We seized these polytheists with our punishment, sent down upon them our torment and wrath, restricted their provisions, made their land barren and killed their leaders by the sword (but they did not humble themselves to their Lord), they did not submit to their Lord by following His commands and reverting to His obedience. (Nor did they supplicate in humility), they were not subservient to Him. Al-Tabari: 19/60.\nAllah sends down His punishment upon disobedient people in order to reform them. How?\nوَلَقَدۡ أَخَذۡنَٰهُم بِٱلۡعَذَابِ فَمَا ٱسۡتَكَانُواْ لِرَبِّهِمۡ وَمَا يَتَضَرَّعُونَ ٧٦ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا فَتَحۡنَا عَلَيۡهِم بَابٗا ذَا عَذَابٖ شَدِيدٍ إِذَا هُمۡ فِيهِ مُبۡلِسُونَ ٧٧\n(Nor did they supplicate in humility), or acknowledge their need for Him; rather they went through it, then they recovered as if nothing had happened to them, and they continued in their misguidance and disbelief. But ahead of them is a punishment that cannot be warded off, as Allah says, (Until when We have opened before them a door of severe punishment). Al-Saadi: 556.\nHeedlessness to warning signs leads to torment afterward. Explain, given this verse.\nوَهُوَ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَنشَأَ لَكُمُ ٱلسَّمۡعَ وَٱلۡأَبۡصَٰرَ وَٱلۡأَفۡـِٔدَةَۚ قَلِيلٗا مَّا تَشۡكُرُونَ ٧٨\nAllah mentions hearing, sight, and hearts because of their immense benefits, hence, thanks must be offered to their Creator. Thanking Allah is believing in His Oneness, and following His Messenger (ﷺ). Mentioning them is counting the blessings and making a case for the religion. Ibn Juzay: 2/76.\nAmong all organs of the body, Allah singles out these three organs, why? What benefit is gained in mentioning them?\nقُل لِّمَنِ ٱلۡأَرۡضُ وَمَن فِيهَآ إِن كُنتُمۡ تَعۡلَمُونَ ٨٤ سَيَقُولُونَ لِلَّهِۚ قُلۡ أَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُونَ ٨٥ قُلۡ مَن رَّبُّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ ٱلسَّبۡعِ وَرَبُّ ٱلۡعَرۡشِ ٱلۡعَظِيمِ ٨٦ سَيَقُولُونَ لِلَّهِۚ قُلۡ أَفَلَا تَتَّقُونَ ٨٧\nThese verses prove that debating the disbelievers and making good arguments against them is permitted. Al-Qurtubi: 15/80.\nIs it permitted for a knowledgeable person to debate the disbelievers to guide them?\nوَهُوَ يُجِيرُ وَلَا يُجَارُ عَلَيۡهِ\n(And He protects) whomever He wills; He protects whomever He wants so that no one can harm him. (While none can protect against Him), no one can shield someone whom Allah wants to afflict with adversity. Al-Jaza’iri: 3/535.\nThe verse contains assurance to the believer. Explain.\nوَهُوَ يُجِيرُ وَلَا يُجَارُ عَلَيۡهِ\nMeaning: Allah protects, and no one can be shielded against Him. It is said: (He protects), He safeguards whomever He wills. (While none can protect against Him), no one can safeguard another whom Allah wants to destroy. When Allah wants to destroy someone, none can stop that, and when Allah wants to help and safeguard someone, none can keep that from happening. Al-Qurtubi: 15/79.\nHow can you benefit from knowing the meaning of this verse?\nwords\nلَلَجُّواThey would persist\nيَعمَهُونَWandering blindly\nاستَكَانُواThey humbled themselves\nمُبلِسُونَThey will be in despair\nذَرَأَكُمHe created, and multiplied you\nيُجِيرُHe protects and\nوَلاَ يُجَارُ عَلَيهِNone can protect against Him"],[348,"§Al-Mu'minun\ndeeds\nShow kindness to those who wronged you by forgiving and gifting them.\nSeek refuge with Allah in your prostration from the incitements of devils.\nThink of a righteous deed that you kept putting off, and hasten to do it before death comes, and ask Allah for a good end of life.\nguid\nIt is best to repel evil deeds and words by forgiving and turning away from its doer.\nDo not be oblivious to that precious time when the disbeliever wishes he come back to life to please Allah.\nHow can one be proud of his color and lineage when he knows that kinship ties will be irrelevant on the Day of Resurrection; they will never be considered nor will they be looked at.\nrefl\nمَا ٱتَّخَذَ ٱللَّهُ مِن وَلَدٖ وَمَا كَانَ مَعَهُۥ مِنۡ إِلَٰهٍۚ إِذٗا لَّذَهَبَ كُلُّ إِلَٰهِۢ بِمَا خَلَقَ وَلَعَلَا بَعۡضُهُمۡ عَلَىٰ بَعۡضٖۚ سُبۡحَٰنَ ٱللَّهِ عَمَّا يَصِفُونَ ٩١\nThis is a proof of the Oneness of Allah, and it is stated as follows: If there was another god with Allah, then each would separate his creations from the other, dominate his own kingdom and seek to overpower the other to have the upper hand, similar to what you see happening with the kings on earth. However, since, we see that all creatures are linked together as if the whole universe is a single entity, we come to the realization that its creator and the governor of its affairs must be one, no god but Him. Ibn Juzay: 2/77.\nExplain the logical proof of the Oneness of Allah in this verse.\nٱدۡفَعۡ بِٱلَّتِي هِيَ أَحۡسَنُ ٱلسَّيِّئَةَۚ نَحۡنُ أَعۡلَمُ بِمَا يَصِفُونَ ٩٦\nTo practice the meaning of this verse, the ideal believer, when someone wrongs him, should entrust the affair to Allah because He will retaliate for those who rely on Him.Ibn Ashur: 18/120.\nHow does the believer practice the meaning of this verse? Explain.\nٱدۡفَعۡ بِٱلَّتِي هِيَ أَحۡسَنُ ٱلسَّيِّئَةَۚ نَحۡنُ أَعۡلَمُ بِمَا يَصِفُونَ ٩٦ وَقُل رَّبِّ أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنۡ هَمَزَٰتِ ٱلشَّيَٰطِينِ ٩٧\n(Repel evil with what is best), this is what is expected of the pious servant in response to people who mistreat him. As for devils who mistreat humans, kindness is of no benefit in this case, for satan only calls his party to be the inhabitants of the blazing fire. So, what is expected (of humans) in response to him is to follow the instructions given by Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ) by saying, (My Lord, I seek refuge in You from the incitements of the devils). Al-Saadi: 559.\nHow do you repel evil from people? How do you repel evil from devils?\nوَقُل رَّبِّ أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنۡ هَمَزَٰتِ ٱلشَّيَٰطِينِ ٩٧\nAllah commanded His Prophet (ﷺ) and the believers to seek refuge with Him from the incitements of the devil, which are outbursts of anger when man cannot control himself. Al-Qurtubi: 15/83.\nWhat are the devils' incitements from which the servant is commanded to seek refuge? Why was he commanded to do so?\nحَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا جَآءَ أَحَدَهُمُ ٱلۡمَوۡتُ قَالَ رَبِّ ٱرۡجِعُونِ ٩٩ لَعَلِّيٓ أَعۡمَلُ صَٰلِحٗا فِيمَا تَرَكۡتُۚ\nThis verse proves that at the time of death, everyone will surely know whether he is among Allah's allies or one of His enemies; if this were not the case, he would not ask to be sent back. Al-Qurtubi: 15/86.\nAt the time of his death, does the servant know his position with Allah?\nفَإِذَا نُفِخَ فِي ٱلصُّورِ فَلَآ أَنسَابَ بَيۡنَهُمۡ يَوۡمَئِذٖ وَلَا يَتَسَآءَلُونَ ١٠١\n(No kinship ties will there be among them), on that Day, all sympathy and compassion among relatives will vanish because each one of them will be preoccupied with himself, as Allah says, (on that Day everyone will flee from his brother ` and from his mother and father) [80:34-35], so, all kinship ties will be nullified. (Nor will they ask about one another), they will not ask about each other since every one will be engaged with himself. If one asks: How to reconcile the above verse with this one: (They will turn to one another with questions) [37:27]? The answer is: When the Horn is blown with the first blast, they will not ask about one another, but after that, they will, because the Day of Resurrection will be very long, and it will have many standings. Ibn Juzay: 2/79.\nHow do you reconcile verses that confirm asking in the Hereafter and others that do not?\nفَمَن ثَقُلَتۡ مَوَٰزِينُهُۥ فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡمُفۡلِحُونَ ١٠٢\nMeaning: The successful is one whose good deeds outweigh his bad deeds, even by one deed. This was the view of Ibn Abbas (k). Ibn Kathir: 3/249.\nGiven this verse, explain the importance of increasing your good deeds.\nwords\nعَمَّا يَصِفُونَAscribing partners and a son to Allah\nهَمَزَاتِ الشَّيَاطِينِIncitements and whispers of the devils\nبَرزَخٌA barrier, keeping them from returning back\nتَلفَحُIt scorches\nكَالِحُونَTheir lips having been contracted by scorching until their teeth are exposed"],[349,"§Al-Mu'minun\ndeeds\nSay this supplication: [Our Lord, we have believed, so forgive us and have mercy upon us, and You are the best of the merciful].\nAdvise someone who mocks religious people and preachers, and recite this verse to him.\nWarn your family and those around you against deeds and sayings that lead to shirk, and explain the risk of committing them.\nguid\nBeware of mocking righteous people.\nPatience in relation to faith is like the head in relation to the body.\nYour life is short no matter how long you live; so endure all pain and hardships for the sake of Allah.\nrefl\nقَالُواْ رَبَّنَا غَلَبَتۡ عَلَيۡنَا شِقۡوَتُنَا\nMeaning: Evidence has been established against us, but we were so wretched that we could not follow it. Ibn Kathir: 3/249.\nExplain the risk when wretchedness overwhelms man.\nقَالُواْ رَبَّنَا غَلَبَتۡ عَلَيۡنَا شِقۡوَتُنَا وَكُنَّا قَوۡمٗا ضَآلِّينَ ١٠٦\nThe best meaning said in this: Our lusts and whims overcome us. Lusts and whims are called (wretchedness) because they lead a person to it. It is also said that it means having full trust in oneself and distrust of others. Al-Baghawi: 3/267.\nLusts and whims are called (wretchedness). Why?\nإِنَّهُۥ كَانَ فَرِيقٞ مِّنۡ عِبَادِي يَقُولُونَ رَبَّنَآ ءَامَنَّا فَٱغۡفِرۡ لَنَا وَٱرۡحَمۡنَا وَأَنتَ خَيۡرُ ٱلرَّٰحِمِينَ ١٠٩ فَٱتَّخَذۡتُمُوهُمۡ سِخۡرِيًّا حَتَّىٰٓ أَنسَوۡكُمۡ ذِكۡرِي وَكُنتُم مِّنۡهُمۡ تَضۡحَكُونَ ١١٠\nThis verse contains a warning against mocking, ridiculing and belittling the oppressed and the weak, and becoming distracted by doing that to no avail, which takes a person away from Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 15/95.\nIn light of this verse, explain the risk of mocking and ridiculing the oppressed.\nإِنَّهُۥ كَانَ فَرِيقٞ مِّنۡ عِبَادِي يَقُولُونَ رَبَّنَآ ءَامَنَّا فَٱغۡفِرۡ لَنَا وَٱرۡحَمۡنَا وَأَنتَ خَيۡرُ ٱلرَّٰحِمِينَ ١٠٩ فَٱتَّخَذۡتُمُوهُمۡ سِخۡرِيًّا حَتَّىٰٓ أَنسَوۡكُمۡ ذِكۡرِي وَكُنتُم مِّنۡهُمۡ تَضۡحَكُونَ ١١٠\n(Indeed, there was a group of My servants), the use of the word (indeed) confirms that the real reasons for entering Hellfire is their mockery of the group of believers who used to say, (Our Lord, we have believed, so forgive us and have mercy upon us, and You are the best of the merciful), so the disbelievers mock the oppressed believers in this worldly life until it made them forget Allah's remembrance and the belief in Him, thus, they will enter Hellfire. Al-Shanqiti: 5/360.\nMocking and ridiculing righteous people has a grave consequence, what is it?\nقَٰلَ كَمۡ لَبِثۡتُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ عَدَدَ سِنِينَ ١١٢ قَالُواْ لَبِثۡنَا يَوۡمًا أَوۡ بَعۡضَ يَوۡمٖ فَسۡـَٔلِ ٱلۡعَآدِّينَ ١١٣\nThe purpose of this question is to make them admit to the fact that their lifetimes were short, yet their disbelief through their short lives led them to a very long punishment. Ibn Atiyah: 4/158.\nAllah will ask the dwellers of Hellfire about the time length they spent on earth. Why?\nأَفَحَسِبۡتُمۡ أَنَّمَا خَلَقۡنَٰكُمۡ عَبَثٗا وَأَنَّكُمۡ إِلَيۡنَا لَا تُرۡجَعُونَ ١١٥ فَتَعَٰلَى ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡمَلِكُ ٱلۡحَقُّۖ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ رَبُّ ٱلۡعَرۡشِ ٱلۡكَرِيمِ ١١٦\n(Exalted is Allah), Allah is Glorified, and Most High; He is above this false assumption that discredits His Wisdom. Al-Saadi: 560.\nThe assumption of useless creation is followed by (Exalted is Allah). Why?\nوَمَن يَدۡعُ مَعَ ٱللَّهِ إِلَٰهًا ءَاخَرَ لَا بُرۡهَٰنَ لَهُۥ بِهِۦ فَإِنَّمَا حِسَابُهُۥ عِندَ رَبِّهِۦٓۚ إِنَّهُۥ لَا يُفۡلِحُ ٱلۡكَٰفِرُونَ ١١٧\nNotice how this Surah begins with describing the success of the believers, and concludes with describing the unsuccess of the disbelievers, so that the difference between the two groups becomes quite clear. Ibn Juzay: 2/79.\nWhat is the link between the beginning and the conclusion of this Surah?\nwords\nاخسَأُواRemain despised\nفَاتَّخَذتُمُوهُم سِخرِيًّاYou were busy mocking them\nالعَآدِّينَThose who keep count"],[350,"§An-Nur\ndeeds\nWrite an article or share a message about the risk of adultery on the individual and society.\nExplain in an article or message the harmful effects of the hypocritical agenda which calls, in the media, for the removal of women's veils, gender mixing, and prohibited friendships (between man and woman) instead of marriage.\nGive a talk on the risk of engaging in slandering.\nguid\nThe association of adulterous male and female with the polytheist male and female in marriage shows strong repulsion to adultery.\nAvoid slandering others.\nAllah ordains the prescribed punishments to mend society and protect it from immorality, and grant victory to the oppressed.\nrefl\nٱلزَّانِيَةُ وَٱلزَّانِي فَٱجۡلِدُواْ كُلَّ وَٰحِدٖ مِّنۡهُمَا مِاْئَةَ جَلۡدَةٖۖ وَلَا تَأۡخُذۡكُم بِهِمَا رَأۡفَةٞ فِي دِينِ ٱللَّهِ إِن كُنتُمۡ تُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِۖ وَلۡيَشۡهَدۡ عَذَابَهُمَا طَآئِفَةٞ مِّنَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٢\nThe mention of a female fornicator precedes that of a male fornicator to draw attention to the ruling. Since the woman is mostly the inducer of the man to commit fornication, and with her collaboration, fornication occurs. If she had refrained from that, the man would not have been able to do it. So, she is mentioned first to emphasize warning to her. Ibn Ashur: 18/146.\nThe mention of a female fornicator precedes that of a male fornicator. Why?\nٱلزَّانِيَةُ وَٱلزَّانِي فَٱجۡلِدُواْ كُلَّ وَٰحِدٖ مِّنۡهُمَا مِاْئَةَ جَلۡدَةٖۖ وَلَا تَأۡخُذۡكُم بِهِمَا رَأۡفَةٞ فِي دِينِ ٱللَّهِ إِن كُنتُمۡ تُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِۖ وَلۡيَشۡهَدۡ عَذَابَهُمَا طَآئِفَةٞ مِّنَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٢\nThis, in fact, shows Allah's mercy for His servants since He sent Muhammad (ﷺ) as a mercy to the worlds. Allah, the Exalted, is more merciful to His servants than a mother to her child. However, sometimes, the required mercy does not occur except with some pain and hardship to some souls. Ibn Taimyah: 4/486.\nAllah's mercy to His servants does not occur except with some pain and hardship. Explain in the light of the verse.\nوَلَا تَأۡخُذۡكُم بِهِمَا رَأۡفَةٞ فِي دِينِ ٱللَّهِ\nThis does not mean that we should not naturally feel pity when carrying out the punishment. What is prohibited here is the kind of pity that may make the judge ignore the punishment altogether. This is what is not permitted. Ibn Kathir: 3/253.\nWhat is the forbidden pity in this verse?\nوَلۡيَشۡهَدۡ عَذَابَهُمَا طَآئِفَةٞ مِّنَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٢\nSo that it will become widely known and thus disgrace the fornicators and deter others from committing this deed. Al-Saadi: 561.\nWhat is the benefit of letting people witness the punishment?\nٱلزَّانِي لَا يَنكِحُ إِلَّا زَانِيَةً أَوۡ مُشۡرِكَةٗ وَٱلزَّانِيَةُ لَا يَنكِحُهَآ إِلَّا زَانٍ أَوۡ مُشۡرِكٞۚ وَحُرِّمَ ذَٰلِكَ عَلَى ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٣\nThis highlights the abhorrent nature of fornication, for it tarnishes the honor of the one who does it and that of the one with whom he does it, in a manner that is not shared by other sins. Al-Saadi: 561.\nThe verse indicates the abhorrent nature of fornication. Explain.\nوَٱلَّذِينَ يَرۡمُونَ ٱلۡمُحۡصَنَٰتِ ثُمَّ لَمۡ يَأۡتُواْ بِأَرۡبَعَةِ شُهَدَآءَ فَٱجۡلِدُوهُمۡ ثَمَٰنِينَ جَلۡدَةٗ وَلَا تَقۡبَلُواْ لَهُمۡ شَهَٰدَةً أَبَدٗاۚ وَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡفَٰسِقُونَ ٤\nIn this verse, Allah mentions only women because accusing them of indecency is more hideous and repulsive, but this rule applies also to men, according to the consensus of the Muslim community. Al-Qurtubi: 15/123.\nAllah mentions only women even though it applies also to men. Why?\nوَٱلۡخَٰمِسَةُ أَنَّ لَعۡنَتَ ٱللَّهِ عَلَيۡهِ إِن كَانَ مِنَ ٱلۡكَٰذِبِينَ ٧\nThe wrath of Allah is mentioned specially in the case of the woman because usually a man would not go to the extent of exposing his wife and accusing her of adultery unless he is telling the truth, and has good reason to do this, and that she knows that what he is accusing her of is true. Hence, in her case, the fifth testimony calls for the wrath of Allah to be upon her, for the one upon whom is the wrath of Allah, is the one who knows the truth yet deviates from it. Ibn Kathir: 3/257.\nThe wrath of Allah is mentioned specially in the case of the woman. Why?\nwords\nوَفَرَضنَاهَاWe ordained its laws\nطَائِفَةٌA group\nيَرمُونَThose who accuse\nالمُحصَنَاتِChaste women\nوَيَدرَأُIt will prevent punishment"],[351,"§An-Nur\ndeeds\nRead about the slander incident from Sahih Al-Bukhari, and draw three lessons from it.\nList three measures to stop the spread of bad rumors.\nSuggest a solution to prevent the spread of indecency in the community.\nguid\nAllah's decree for the believer is all good; so do not grieve over what has befallen you, for perhaps it is good for you.\nKeep positive assumptions about your brothers and sisters in Islam.\nSlandering and baseless accusations are tremendous sins and extremely prohibited.\nrefl\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ جَآءُو بِٱلۡإِفۡكِ عُصۡبَةٞ مِّنكُمۡۚ لَا تَحۡسَبُوهُ شَرّٗا لَّكُمۖ بَلۡ هُوَ خَيۡرٞ لَّكُمۡۚ لِكُلِّ ٱمۡرِيٕٖ مِّنۡهُم مَّا ٱكۡتَسَبَ مِنَ ٱلۡإِثۡمِۚ وَٱلَّذِي تَوَلَّىٰ كِبۡرَهُۥ مِنۡهُمۡ لَهُۥ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٞ ١١\n(Rather it is good for you), addressing all Muslims, and the good in it has five aspects: Declaration of innocence of the Mother of the Believers, the honor bestowed upon her by sending down a revelation concerning her, the great reward for her for enduring this slander, admonishment to the believers, and punishment of those were responsible for the slander. Ibn Juzay: 2/84.\nIdentify the aspects of good in this slander event.\nلَّوۡلَآ إِذۡ سَمِعۡتُمُوهُ ظَنَّ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنَٰتُ بِأَنفُسِهِمۡ خَيۡرٗا وَقَالُواْ هَٰذَآ إِفۡكٞ مُّبِينٞ ١٢\nMeaning: The believers (men and women) should have checked this accusation against their own morals; if that was implausible to occur with them, then it was even more so with Aisha (i) due to her virtue. It is narrated that this comparison was done by Abu Ayoub Al-Ansari (t) who said to his wife: \"Would you have done such a thing?\" She replied: \"No, by Allah\", then he said: \"Well, Aisha is better than you\", and she said: \"Yes, indeed.\" Ibn Juzay: 2/85.\nWhat is the Muslim's duty when he hears unpleasant things about righteous people?\nإِذۡ تَلَقَّوۡنَهُۥ بِأَلۡسِنَتِكُمۡ وَتَقُولُونَ بِأَفۡوَاهِكُم مَّا لَيۡسَ لَكُم بِهِۦ عِلۡمٞ وَتَحۡسَبُونَهُۥ هَيِّنٗا وَهُوَ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ عَظِيمٞ ١٥ وَلَوۡلَآ إِذۡ سَمِعۡتُمُوهُ قُلۡتُم مَّا يَكُونُ لَنَآ أَن نَّتَكَلَّمَ بِهَٰذَا سُبۡحَٰنَكَ هَٰذَا بُهۡتَٰنٌ عَظِيمٞ ١٦\n(Received it), means that you take it from one another. In this, and the verse before is a reproach to them for engaging in the slander talk, even though they did not believe it, but they should have refrained from its mention and dropped it altogether. The reproach was for three things, first: Receiving it with the tongue, which means inquiring and receiving it. Second: Uttering it. Third: They thought it was insignificant while it was tremendous in the sight of Allah. Using the words (tongues) and (mouths) indicate that they did not know the truth about it in their hearts. Ibn Juzay: 2/85.\nIn light of this verse, explain the right stand on the rumors about righteous people.\nإِذۡ تَلَقَّوۡنَهُۥ بِأَلۡسِنَتِكُمۡ وَتَقُولُونَ بِأَفۡوَاهِكُم مَّا لَيۡسَ لَكُم بِهِۦ عِلۡمٞ وَتَحۡسَبُونَهُۥ هَيِّنٗا وَهُوَ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ عَظِيمٞ ١٥\nThis verse indicates a high moral etiquette that one should not speak with his tongue that which he does not know. Ibn Ashur: 18/178.\nThis verse indicates an etiquette for speaking. What is it?\nوَتَحۡسَبُونَهُۥ هَيِّنٗا وَهُوَ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ عَظِيمٞ ١٥\nThis is an emphatic rebuke against indulging in some sins because one thinks that they are trivial. However, what a person thinks will not avail him anything and will not reduce the punishment for that sin; rather, it makes him get carried away in sin and makes it easy for him to do it again. Al-Saadi: 564.\nWhat is the risk of taking some sins lightly?\nوَلَوۡلَآ إِذۡ سَمِعۡتُمُوهُ قُلۡتُم مَّا يَكُونُ لَنَآ أَن نَّتَكَلَّمَ بِهَٰذَا سُبۡحَٰنَكَ هَٰذَا بُهۡتَٰنٌ عَظِيمٞ ١٦\nThe scholars said: This verse is a fundamental principle in affirming that the believer's faith, his righteousness, and his chastity cannot be all simply dismissed because of a probable accusation, even if it is widespread, especially if its source is corrupt or unknown. Al-Qurtubi: 15/172.\nWhat should be our stand on the corrupt rumors about righteous people?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يُحِبُّونَ أَن تَشِيعَ ٱلۡفَٰحِشَةُ فِي ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَهُمۡ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٞ فِي ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَٱلۡأٓخِرَةِۚ وَٱللَّهُ يَعۡلَمُ وَأَنتُمۡ لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ١٩\n(Indeed, those who like to see indecency spread), this points to the hypocrites who liked to see the talk about the slander spread in the community. It also applies to others who do the same as they did. Ibn Juzay: 2/85.\nThe verse reveals one of the traits of the hypocrites. What is it?\nwords\nبِالإِفكِThe slander against Aisha (i), wife of the Prophet (ﷺ) and Mother of the Believers\nعُصبَةٌ مِنكُمA group among you\nأَفَضتُم فِيهِYour talk about the slander\nبُهتَانٌA slander\nيَعِظُكُمُHe warns you"],[352,"§An-Nur\ndeeds\nAsk Allah and implore Him to purify your soul.\nShow kindness to someone who wronged you.\nLearn the etiquettes of asking permission, and use them.\nguid\nDo not swear to break ties of kinship or stop doing a good deed; if you did, retract what you said and expiate for your broken oath.\nSlandering chaste, unaware believing women is a major sin.\nRemember that your limbs will testify to your words and deeds on the Day of Resurrection.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَتَّبِعُواْ خُطُوَٰتِ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنِۚ وَمَن يَتَّبِعۡ خُطُوَٰتِ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنِ فَإِنَّهُۥ يَأۡمُرُ بِٱلۡفَحۡشَآءِ وَٱلۡمُنكَرِۚ\nThe words of this verse allude to following satan and adhering to his whispers. It is as saying: Do not follow satan in any action, including the spared and love of indecency. Al-Alusi: 9/320.\nAllah forbids to follow the footsteps of satan instead of mentioning not to follow him directly. Why?\nوَلَوۡلَا فَضۡلُ ٱللَّهِ عَلَيۡكُمۡ وَرَحۡمَتُهُۥ مَا زَكَىٰ مِنكُم مِّنۡ أَحَدٍ أَبَدٗا وَلَٰكِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُزَكِّي مَن يَشَآءُۗ وَٱللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٞ ٢١\nMost interpreters apply the meaning of this verse in general, saying: Allah says that if not for His favor and mercy through His protection, no one of you would ever be righteous. Al-Baghawi: 3/281.\nCan anyone protect himself from making a mistake?\nوَلَا يَأۡتَلِ أُوْلُواْ ٱلۡفَضۡلِ مِنكُمۡ وَٱلسَّعَةِ أَن يُؤۡتُوٓاْ أُوْلِي ٱلۡقُرۡبَىٰ وَٱلۡمَسَٰكِينَ وَٱلۡمُهَٰجِرِينَ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۖ وَلۡيَعۡفُواْ وَلۡيَصۡفَحُوٓاْۗ أَلَا تُحِبُّونَ أَن يَغۡفِرَ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمۡۚ وَٱللَّهُ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٌ ٢٢\nThis verse was revealed when Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq (t) swore to stop his financial help to his poor cousin, Mistah bin Athathah, for he took part in the slander. After this verse was revealed, Abu Bakr resumed his assistance to him, and expiated his oath. Some scholars said: \"This is the most promising verse in the Quran because Allah recommends kindness to a slanderer.\" It also indicates that no one should swear not to do good. (Would you not like that Allah should forgive you), just as you like Allah to forgive your sins, you should forgive others when they wronged you. After this verse was revealed, Abu Bakr (t) said: \"Indeed, I like Allah to forgive me,\" and he resumed his financial assistance to Mistah. Ibn Juzay: 2/87.\nDo the mistakes of others toward you necessitate abandoning doing good to them?\nوَلۡيَعۡفُواْ وَلۡيَصۡفَحُوٓاْۗ أَلَا تُحِبُّونَ أَن يَغۡفِرَ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمۡۚ وَٱللَّهُ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٌ ٢٢\nThis verse shows that the reward fits the deed, and that if you forgive others, you will be forgiven. Ibn Kathir: 3/267.\nIn light of this verse, talk about the principle of (a befitting recompense).\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَرۡمُونَ ٱلۡمُحۡصَنَٰتِ ٱلۡغَٰفِلَٰتِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنَٰتِ لُعِنُواْ فِي ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ وَلَهُمۡ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٞ ٢٣\nThe (unaware) is the woman who never thinks of committing indecency, and Aisha (i) was just that. Al-Baghawi: 3/282.\nHow can someone be unaware of committing indecency?\nيَوۡمَ تَشۡهَدُ عَلَيۡهِمۡ أَلۡسِنَتُهُمۡ وَأَيۡدِيهِمۡ وَأَرۡجُلُهُم بِمَا كَانُواْ يَعۡمَلُونَ ٢٤\nThese limbs participate in slandering chaste women; their tongues speak the slander, their hands point to the accused women, and their feet carry them to sitting places of people to tell them about the slander. Ibn Ashur: 18/191.\nOf all body limbs, why are these three singled out for mention?\nٱلۡخَبِيثَٰتُ لِلۡخَبِيثِينَ وَٱلۡخَبِيثُونَ لِلۡخَبِيثَٰتِۖ وَٱلطَّيِّبَٰتُ لِلطَّيِّبِينَ وَٱلطَّيِّبُونَ لِلطَّيِّبَٰتِۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ مُبَرَّءُونَ مِمَّا يَقُولُونَۖ لَهُم مَّغۡفِرَةٞ وَرِزۡقٞ كَرِيمٞ ٢٦\nAbu Al-Sa'ib Al-Qadi: I was at the presence of Al-Hasan bin Zayd, and there was a man present with him, who talked about Aisha (i), and slandered her with indecency. Al-Hasan bin Zayd said to his guard: \"Behead this man.\" Al-Hasan's relatives said to him: \"This man is one of our supporters.\" He replied: \"Allah forbid, this man slandered the Prophet (ﷺ), since Allah says, (Evil women are for evil men and evil men for evil women, and virtuous women are for virtuous men and virtuous men for virtuous women. These [virtuous ones] are innocent of what [the slanderers] say; they will have forgiveness and a generous provision). Hence, if Aisha (i) was evil, so was the Prophet (ﷺ); this man is a disbeliever; behead him,\" and he was beheaded while I was present. Narrated by Al-Lalaka'i. Ibn Taimyah: 4/505.\nSlandering the Mother of the believers, Aisha (i), is slandering the Prophet (ﷺ). Explain\nwords\nمَا زَكَىNone would have been pure\nوَلاَ يَأتَلِLet not them swear\nأُولُو الفَضلِThose of virtue and wealth\nالغَافِلاَتِChaste women who never think of indecency\nتَستَأنِسُواYou ask permission of the house owner"],[353,"§An-Nur\ndeeds\nDo your utmost today to lower your gaze toward what is prohibited by Allah.\nShare a message in which you explain the benefits of lowering the gaze toward what Allah prohibited, especially when using new technical devices.\nHasten to repent to Allah today from all your sins.\nguid\nRemember that Allah knows what you reveal and what you conceal, so beware of Him seeing you doing something that displeases Him.\nRepentance from sins bring success in this life and in the Hereafter.\nThe spread of wearing Hijab is one of the reasons for happiness in the community.\nrefl\nوَإِن قِيلَ لَكُمُ ٱرۡجِعُواْ فَٱرۡجِعُواْۖ هُوَ أَزۡكَىٰ لَكُمۡۚ\nQatadah said: One of the emigrant Companions said: \"I have spent all my life trying to apply this verse, but could not - to seek permission to visit one of my brethren, and he tells me: \"Go back\", and I would do it with delight, for Allah says, (And if it is said to you, \"Go back,\" then go back; it is purer for you)\". Al-Tabari: 19/150.\nIf you seek permission to visit, but were told to go back; how would you feel about it?\nقُل لِّلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ يَغُضُّواْ مِنۡ أَبۡصَٰرِهِمۡ وَيَحۡفَظُواْ فُرُوجَهُمۡۚ ذَٰلِكَ أَزۡكَىٰ لَهُمۡۚ\nSight is the biggest gate to the heart, and the most used of all faculties to it, hence, most sins come through the use of sight, hence it is necessary to warn against the improper use of it. It is obligated to lower one's gaze toward forbidden things, or anything that may lead to committing sins. Al-Qurtubi: 15/203.\nExplain the importance of sight and the risk of its misuse.\nقُل لِّلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ يَغُضُّواْ مِنۡ أَبۡصَٰرِهِمۡ وَيَحۡفَظُواْ فُرُوجَهُمۡۚ ذَٰلِكَ أَزۡكَىٰ لَهُمۡۚ\nWhoever gives up something for the sake of Allah, Allah will compensate him with something better, so whoever averts his gaze from what is forbidden, Allah will give him enlightenment. If a person restrains his carnal desires, averts his gaze from what is forbidden, and that which leads to it, despite the pressure of desire, he is more likely to refrain from other things. Therefore, Allah describes this as (guard) because if a person does not try hard to keep watch over the thing that he is guarding, and take proper measures to guard it, it will not be guarded. The same applies to the gaze and carnal desires: if he does not try hard to guard and restrain them, they will cause him to fall into trials and tribulations. Al-Saadi: 566.\nMention two benefits of averting one’s gaze from what is forbidden.\nوَلَا يُبۡدِينَ زِينَتَهُنَّ إِلَّا مَا ظَهَرَ مِنۡهَاۖ\nAllah prohibited revealing the adornments themselves in order to be known that if gazing at them is prohibited because of the body parts on which they are put, then, gazing at the actual body parts is extremely prohibited. This affirms the women's right to cover them, and never expose them due to their fear of Allah. Al-Alusi: 9/335.\nWhat is the benefit of prohibiting the revealing of adornment?\nوَلَا يَضۡرِبۡنَ بِأَرۡجُلِهِنَّ لِيُعۡلَمَ مَا يُخۡفِينَ مِن زِينَتِهِنَّۚ\nFrom this verse and others, the principle of barring the means is derived. If something is permissible in and of itself, but it may lead to something that is prohibited, or there is the fear that it may happen, then it is disallowed. Stamping the feet on the ground is permissible in principle, but if it is a means of making hidden adornment known, then it is disallowed. Al-Saadi: 567.\nWhat is the fundamental principle derived from this verse?\nوَتُوبُوٓاْ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ جَمِيعًا أَيُّهَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ ٣١\nRepentance to Allah is a duty upon every adult believer, which is inferred by the Quran, Sunnah, and the consensus of Ummah. There are three conditions for repentance, first: Regretting the sin, in the sense that it was a disobedience of the Lord of Majesty and not because of harm done to health or wealth. Second: Quitting the sin as soon as possible, without further delay or wait. Third: Making a resolve never to go back to that sin again. There are three etiquettes for repentance, first: Admitting, with humility, to the sin. Second: Imploring Allah often and asking for His forgiveness. Third: Doing more good deeds often to erase past evil deeds. Ibn Juzay: 2/90.\nMention the conditions for repentance, and give an example of admitting, with humility, to the sin from the supplication of Prophet Jonah (u).\nوَتُوبُوٓاْ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ جَمِيعًا أَيُّهَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ ٣١\nThere are seven incentives for someone to repent: Fear of punishment, hope for the reward, feeling of shame in facing reckoning, love of Allah, consciousness of the Near, the Watchful [Allah], glorifying Allah's position, and being grateful to the blessings. Ibn Juzay: 2/90.\nWhat are the incentives for someone to repent?\nwords\nإِلاَّ مَا ظَهَرَ مِنهَاThe outer clothes\nعَلَى جُيُوبِهِنَّOver their chests, in order to cover their faces\nلِبُعُولَتِهِنَّTheir husbands\nغَيرِ أُولِي الإِربَةِMen who have no physical desire in women"]])